      "summary": "Good afternoon Stella, How are you? Just wanted to check in as we haven't spoken in about a week. I've been pretty busy lately. I spent a full day filming with Max, so I now have a lot of content to edit and upload over the coming weeks. We're also talking abo",
      "body": "Good afternoon Stella,\n\nHow are you? Just wanted to check in as we haven't spoken in about a week.\n\nI've been pretty busy lately. I spent a full day filming with Max, so I now\nhave a lot of content to edit and upload over the coming weeks. We're also\ntalking about doing some future collaborations, which I think could make\nfor some really strong content on the channel.\n\nAlongside that, I've got plans for some product reviews, tutorials, shorts\nand streaming, so there's plenty in the pipeline.\n\nI also wanted to follow up regarding the course. I've started putting it\ntogether and have already had the first session with the student. I was\njust wondering whether the Evo unit has been shipped to him yet and if you\nhave the tracking number?\n\nAlso, let me know when you have some free time. It would be great to catch\nup and go over the course together.\n\nFinally, a quick update on the Melbourne Junior tournament. The organiser\nhas purchased a Chessnut Move and has been showing it off around the club,\nso that's been some nice promotion already. He's also shared the planned\nvenue layout with me, including the booth location and visibility, giving\nus the best location right outside the playing hall.\n\nSince the event is still a few months away, I was wondering whether you'd\nbe interested in having a pull-up banner made for the booth. If you're\nhappy with the idea, I can contact a few local printing companies and get\nthe dimensions and pricing. It looks like they'd cost around AUD $300–400.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you!\n\nRegards,\nWade\n\nGood afternoon Stella,\nHow are you? Just wanted to check in as we haven&#39;t spoken in about a week.\nI&#39;ve been pretty busy lately. I spent a full day filming with Max, so I now have a lot of content to edit and upload over the coming weeks. We&#39;re also talking about doing some future collaborations, which I think could make for some really strong content on the channel.\nAlongside 