      "email": "gadgetify@gmail.com",
      "subject": "Re: 回复：回复：Chessnut July Updates – Sale, Companion & New App",
      "summary": "Good morning Stella, Just wanted to get back to you on this. These were very helpful. We were able to link our Stockfish 18 Puzzle Miner app to Chessnut Move and Chessnut Go boards. Quite amazing how well it works! We will post the videos to our channel soon. ",
      "body": "Good morning Stella,\n\nJust wanted to get back to you on this. These were very helpful. We were\nable to link our Stockfish 18 Puzzle Miner app to Chessnut Move and\nChessnut Go boards. Quite amazing how well it works! We will post the\nvideos to our channel soon. Thanks again for this.\n\nKind Regards,\n\nCyrus\n\nOn 7/9/2026 4:28 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n> Hi Cyrus,\n>\n> Thanks for your interest in integrating with Chessnut boards.\n> Here are two documentation links that should be helpful for your\n> development:\n> Chessnut eBoards API (for Air, Air+, Go, Pro):\n> https://github.com/chessnutech/Chessnut_eBoards\n> This covers Bluetooth connection, FEN data retrieval, LED control, and\n> battery reading for our non-Move boards.\n> Chessnut Move API (for the Move board):\n> https://github.com/chessnutech/chess_move_api\n> This includes everything from the eBoards API, plus additional\n> features specific to the Move board, such as setting FEN for auto-move\n> functionality, reading piece status, and more detailed LED color control.\n> Both repositories are public and contain code examples to help you get\n> started. Let us know if you have any questions during development!\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：Gadgetify\n> 发送时间：2026年7月7日(周二) 22:10\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: 回复：Chessnut July Updates – Sale, Companion & New App\n>\n> Thank you Stella! Right now, we are working on a comprehensive app\n> that runs Stockfish 24/7 to find / come up with never seen before\n> puzzles and studies. We have worked very hard on it, but we would\n> love to be able to interface it with Chessnut and other boards!\n> Any documentation that could help us is very much appreciated!\n>\n> Best,\n>\n> Cyrus\n>\n> Gadgetify\n>\n> On 7/7/2026 5:11 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n> Hi Cyrus,\n>\n> Thanks for your message — glad to hear you’re excited about the\n> Companion.\n> We can definitely add you to the list and send one over once we\n> have stock available. I’ll let you know as soon as it’s ready to ship.\n> As for the custom app development question — I’ll check with our\n> tech team and get back to you on that.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：Gadgetify\n> 发送时间：2026年7月1日(周三) 06:03\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut July Updates – Sale, Companion & New App\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Great update. We would love to test the Chessnut Companion if it\n> is possible. I think we won a prize from you for being one of the\n> most active Chessnut posters? If you need tons of videos for the\n> Chessnut Companion, we can certainly deliver on that. I think it\n> would go great with the Chessnut Move.  We have done reviews of\n> DGT Pi in the past but this looks 100x times better. Very\n> exciting! One question: is it codable? Can we develop custom apps\n> for it?\n>\n> Kind Regards,\n>\n> Cyrus\n>\n> Gadgetify\n>\n> On 6/30/2026 5:39 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n> Hi everyone,\n>\n> Long time no see — a few quick updates:\n>\n> 1. 6th Anniversary Sale (July 1–11)\n> 20% off storewide — your discount codes work too. We’ve been\n> running fewer discounts this year, so this is a good one to plan\n> content around. Good for board reviews, accessories, or anything\n> you want to feature. If you need us to boost anything, just send\n> the link.\n>\n> 2. Chessnut Companion Launch – July 3, 8:00 AM EST\n> First batch: 200 units at 20% off → $367.20.\n> Key features:\n> - AI coaching & real-time guidance\n> - Tournament-grade chess clock\n> - Voice control\n> - Works with Chess.com, Lichess, and more\n> - Motorized auto-switch\n> Compatible with all Chessnut boards except Evo. Only 200 units\n> available at this price, so it’s worth acting early. Interested?\n> Submit your content ideas — we’ll review them.\n>\n> 3. Chessnut Next – App Overhaul\n> We’re rolling out a completely redesigned app that turns the\n> Chessnut board into a full training ecosystem:\n> - Daily Task & Career mode — Gamified progression with tasks,\n> points, ELO, bosses, and challenges to keep you engaged every day.\n> - Maia3 integration — The latest human‑style AI engine helps you\n> understand why players at different levels tend to make certain\n> moves, not just what the best move is.\n> - Multiple analysis reports — Standard / Stockfish, Grandeur, and\n> Maia3 Human Review — so you can review the same game from three\n> angles: objective engine, coach-level explanation, and human‑style\n> insight.\n> - Progress tools — Mistake Book, themed puzzles, interactive\n> lessons, and Board Analyzer turn each game review into actionable\n> practice.\n> It’s currently in beta. If you’re interested in participating,\n> just let me know.\n>\n> Let me know if you have any questions!\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n>\n--------------HN0ufKjWM0ai2D8R0LdLFENv\nContent-Type: multipart/related;\nboundary=\"------------OqXchgpcvAtaGs3jKE000QN1\"\n\n--------------OqXchgpcvAtaGs3jKE000QN1\nContent-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8\nContent-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n\nGood morning Stella,\nJust wanted to get back to you on this. These were very helpful.\nWe were able to link our Stockfish 18 Puzzle Miner app to Chessnut\nMove and Chessnut Go boards. Quite amazing how well it works! We\nwill post the videos to our channel soon. Thanks again for this.\nKind Regards,\nCyrus\nOn 7/9/2026 4:28 AM, Stella Zhuang\nwrote:\n\nHi\nCyrus,\n\nThanks for your interest in\nintegrating with Chessnut boards.\nHere are two documentation links\nthat should be helpful for your development:\nChessnut eBoards API (for Air,\nAir+, Go, Pro):\nhttps://github.com/chessnutech/Chessnut_eBoards\nThis covers Bluetooth connection,\nFEN data retrieval, LED control, and battery reading for\nour non-Move boards.\nChessnut Move API (for the Move\nboard):\nhttps://github.com/chessnutech/chess_move_api\nThis includes everything from the\neBoards API, plus additional features specific to the Move\nboard, such as setting FEN for auto-move functionality,\nreading piece status, and more detailed LED color control.\nBoth repositories are public and contain code examples\nto help you get started. Let us know if you have any\nquestions during development!\n\nBest,\nStella\nBusiness Development Manager | Chessnut\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\n发件人：Gadgetify\n&lt;gadgetify@gmail.com&gt;\n发送时间：2026年7月7日(周二) 22:10\n收件人：Stella\nZhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt;\n主　题：Re: 回复：Chessnut July Updates\n– Sale, Companion &amp; New App\n\nThank\nyou Stella! Right now, we are working on a comprehensive\napp that runs Stockfish 24/7 to find / come up with\nnever seen before puzzles and studies. We have worked\nvery hard on it, but we would love to be able to\ninterface it with Chessnut and other boards! Any\ndocumentation that could help us is very much\nappreciated!\nBest,\nCyrus\nGadgetify\nOn 7/7/2026 5:11 AM, Stella\nZhuang wrote:\n\nHi\nCyrus,\n\nThanks for your message\n— glad to hear you’re excited about the\nCompanion.\nWe can definitely add\nyou to the list and send one over once we have\nstock available. I’ll let you know as soon as\nit’s ready to ship.\nAs for the custom app development question —\nI’ll check with our tech team and get back to\nyou on that.\n\nBest,\nStella\nBusiness Development Manager | Chessnut\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\n发件人：Gadgetify &lt;gadgetify@gmail.com&gt;\n发送时间：2026年7月1日(周三)\n06:03\n收件人：Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt;\n主　题：Re: Chessnut July\nUpdates – Sale, Companion &amp; New App\n\nHi\nStella,\nGreat\nupdate. We would love to test the Chessnut\nCompanion if it is possible. I think we won a\nprize from you for being one of the most\nactive Chessnut posters? If you need tons of\nvideos for the Chessnut Companion, we can\ncertainly deliver on that. I think it would go\ngreat with the Chessnut Move.  We have done\nreviews of DGT Pi in the past but this looks\n100x times better. Very exciting! One\nquestion: is it codable? Can we develop custom\napps for it?\nKind\nRegards,\nCyrus\nGadgetify\nOn 6/30/2026 5:39\nAM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n\nHi\neveryone,\n\nLong time no\nsee — a few quick updates:\n\n1. 6th\nAnniversary Sale (July 1–11)\n20% off\nstorewide — your discount codes work\ntoo. We’ve been running fewer\ndiscounts this year, so this is a\ngood one to plan content around.\nGood for board reviews, accessories,\nor anything you want to feature. If\nyou need us to boost anything, just\nsend the link.\n\n2.\nChessnut Companion Launch – July\n3, 8:00 AM EST\nFirst batch:\n200 units at 20% off → $367.20.\nKey\nfeatures:\n- AI\ncoaching &amp; real-time guidance\n-\nTournament-grade chess clock\n- Voice\ncontrol\n- Works with\nChess.com, Lichess, and more\n- Motorized\nauto-switch\nCompatible\nwith all Chessnut boards except Evo.\nOnly 200 units available at this\nprice, so it’s worth acting early.\nInterested? Submit your content\nideas — we’ll review them.\n\n3.\nChessnut Next – App Overhaul\nWe’re\nrolling out a completely redesigned\napp that turns the Chessnut board\ninto a full training ecosystem:\n- Daily Task\n&amp; Career mode — Gamified\nprogression with tasks, points, ELO,\nbosses, and challenges to keep you\nengaged every day.\n- Maia3\nintegration — The latest human‑style\nAI engine helps you understand why\nplayers at different levels tend to\nmake certain moves, not just what\nthe best move is.\n- Multiple\nanalysis reports — Standard /\nStockfish, Grandeur, and Maia3 Human\nReview — so you can review the same\ngame from three angles: objective\nengine, coach-level explanation, and\nhuman‑style insight.\n- Progress\ntools — Mistake Book, themed\npuzzles, interactive lessons, and\nBoard Analyzer turn each game review\ninto actionable practice.\nIt’s\ncurrently in beta. If you’re\ninterested in participating, just\nlet me know.\n\nLet me know if you have any\nquestions!\n\nBest,\nStella\nBusiness Development Manager |\nChessnut\n\n--------------OqXchgpcvAtaGs3jKE000QN1\nContent-Type: image/png; name=\"temp4cj.png\"\nContent-Disposition: inline; filename=\"temp4cj.png\"\nContent-Id:\nContent-Transfer-Encoding: base64\n\niVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAApoAAANwCAYAAACPpMqvAAAgAElEQVR4nOydeXRcxZX/v/16\n71a31NosWau12bJkW5Ll3XjBGAPGCzH7hEBghi3kJGROMoFMZhJmJnOSyWSGBAayAYGwBDAE\nzGITg3FsbORdtiRLlmy0WNa+97693x8+t1z93LJFglh+uZ9zdCR1v/eqXlW9qm/de6ueDoAK\nhmGYzwCdTgdFUaCqKlT1bFekKAqi0aj42263Izc3FwUFBUhLS0N+fj7S0tKQk5ODzMxMJCYm\nYmxsDG+//TZ+9rOfoa+vD0ajUVwjGo1Cp9OJvxmGYZhPD8NnnQGGYf52IaEZDoeh0+nE/4qi\nwOVyoaCgADNnzkRVVRWqqqpQUlICq9WKEydOwOFwIDU1FUajEcePH8drr72GoaEhGAwGhEIh\n6HQ6GI1GAICqqkJsMgzDMJ8eLDQZhvnMICumwWAQYtDpdCInJwdLlizBxo0bsXDhQpjNZoyM\njKCrqwsdHR3YunUrqqursXjxYthsNnR1daGrqwvRaBQ2mw1+vx+qqgrraCQS+YzvlGEY5m8T\nFpoMw3xmkBXTZDLB7/fD5XJh48aNuP3221FRUYFoNAq3242Ojg688847ePLJJ9HS0gKdToeC\nggLYbDa4XC4sWbIEt956K371q1/B5/MhISEBHo8HoVBICE7ZPc8wDMN8eqj8wz/8wz+T9aPX\n6+N+riiKajabVavVqur1erWwsFB9+umn1YGBAVVVVTUSiagNDQ3qAw88oGZmZqo6nU61WCxq\namqqmpiYqK5cuVJ94okn1K6uLlVVVTUYDKq1tbXqqlWrVIPBoKampqoWi0U1GAwiDzqd7jMv\nD/7hH/7hn7+lHz2AH4BhGGYS0Ol00Ov1wpJoMpkAnHWV6/V6hMNhmM1mLFmyBE8++SQWLVqE\nhIQEBINBvPDCC/jhD3+ILVu2YHR0FGazGX6/H36/H5FIBF1dXThy5AiOHTuGaDSKwsJCTJky\nBcuXL0cgEEB9fT28Xq9In1zzHKvJMAzz6cFCk2GYSUdVVej1ehiNRuh0Oqiqimg0iqSkJFx5\n5ZX4yU9+guLiYphMJpw6dQoPPfQQfvvb36K5uRkejwfRaDRmxXg0GkU4HMbY2Bja29tx5MgR\nNDQ0wOVyoby8HEajEe+99x6Gh4dZXDIMw3yGcIwmwzCThmzRjEajCAaDsFqtiEQicDqduOqq\nq3DfffchIyMD4XAY+/fvx29+8xu888476O/vh9FoFJbMaDQKk8kEnU6HYDAoxGsoFMLJkyfR\n09OD4eFhLFu2DJWVlUhLS0N3dzfC4TCi0WhMfCaJXYZhGGZyUT7rDDAM8/8nZEkkSyRZFUOh\nkHCX33rrrSgrKwMA7N69Gw8//DD+9Kc/YWxsDGazGTqdTqwYV1UVkUgE4XBYiET6zmg0wu/3\n49ixY2hqaoLL5cK8efOQmJiIaDQKRVFgMBhiLJts6WQYhpl82HXOMMykoBVyer1exGXOmjUL\nt9xyCy6//HJEIhG0tbXh5z//Od5++214vV6x