      "bodyChinese": "Dear Stella,\n\nThank you for the update, and no worries about the delay.\n\nThe proposed framework sounds great from our side, and I believe it\nprovides a strong foundation for a long-term partnership. We appreciate\nyour openness and look forward to hearing from you once you've discussed\nthe remaining details with your team.\n\nBest regards,\n\nOn Fri, Jul 17, 2026 at 1:27 PM Stella Zhuang\nwrote:\n\n> Hi Ammar,\n>\n> Thanks for your follow-up — and sorry for the delay on our side.\n> This project involves quite a few details, so I'll need to discuss it with\n> my team before I can give you a clear answer. That said, I'd like to share\n> my initial thoughts with you, so we can align expectations and move more\n> efficiently once I come back to you.\n> Here's what I have in mind:\n> Products included in the sponsorship: one unit of each product in our\n> lineup.\n> Shipping to the UAE: Chessnut will cover the cost of sending the sponsored\n> units to your location.\n> Customer purchases: shipping costs for customer orders will be covered by\n> the buyers themselves.\n> Partnership duration: we're open to an annual partnership, which would\n> allow us to support multiple events throughout the year.\n> Event support: the level of material support will depend on the scale of\n> each tournament, the number of participants, and the promotional efforts\n> around it — we'll evaluate case by case.\n> For the rest, I'll need to discuss internally with my team before I can\n> confirm anything.\n> In the meantime, I'd love to hear your thoughts on this framework —\n> especially if you have any preferences or suggestions on how we could\n> structure this to work better for both sides. That would help us move\n> faster once we're ready to finalize.\n> I'll get back to you as soon as I have a clearer picture.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：Ammar sbahi\n> 发送时间：2026年7月15日(周三) 22:01\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主 题：Re: Sponsorship Opportunity - Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club\n>\n> Dear Stella,\n>\n> I hope you're doing well.\n>\n> I just wanted to follow up on my previous email regarding the potential\n> partnership between Chessnut and Al Ain Chess Club.\n>\n> We remain very interested in exploring this collaboration and would\n> appreciate any updates regarding the sponsorship details when you have the\n> opportunity.\n>\n> We look forward to hearing from you and hope to move forward together soon.\n>\n> Thank you for your time.\n>\n> On Wed, Jul 8, 2026 at 12:28 PM Ammar sbahi wrote:\n> Dear Stella,\n>\n> Thank you for your thoughtful proposal and for taking the time to outline\n> your vision for a long-term partnership.\n>\n> We truly appreciate the opportunity and believe this could be the\n> beginning of a valuable collaboration between Chessnut and Al Ain Chess\n> Club.\n>\n> We are very interested in the product sponsorship model and the pre-order\n> distribution approach, especially as it allows us to introduce Chessnut\n> products to our community without the need to hold inventory.\n>\n> Before moving forward, we would appreciate a few additional details\n> regarding:\n>\n> - The products included in the sponsorship (models and quantities).\n> - The estimated annual value of the sponsorship.\n> - Whether shipping costs to the UAE are covered by Chessnut.\n> - The distributor margin and ordering process.\n> - Whether the partnership is intended to be annual and include support\n> for multiple tournaments and club activities throughout the year.\n>\n> Once we have these details, we will be pleased to discuss the next steps\n> and work together to establish a successful long-term partnership.\n>\n> We look forward to your response and are excited about the potential\n> opportunities this partnership can create for both Chessnut and Al Ain\n> Chess Club.\n>\n> Best regards,\n>\n>\n> Ammar Sbahi\n> Marketing & Events Coordinator\n>\n> *Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club*\n>\n> Landline: +971 3 763 3387\n>\n> Mobile: +971 56 207 1929\n>\n> Al Ain - United Arab Emirates\n>\n>\n>\n> On Wed, 8 Jul 2026 at 11:49 AM Stella Zhuang stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com> wrote:\n> Dear Ammar,\n>\n> Thanks for your detailed response — it’s clear you’ve put thought into\n> this.\n> On the financial sponsorship side, we’re not able to offer cash support,\n> as Chessnut doesn’t currently have a direct sales channel in the Middle\n> East. However, we do see a number of customers from the region reaching out\n> to us, and they often have no easy way to purchase our products.\n> What we’d like to propose instead is a product-based sponsorship model,\n> combined with a distribution opportunity for your club. Here’s what we have\n> in mind:\n> We can provide product sponsorship — a full set of boards, tournament\n> prizes, and ongoing event support — along with social media promotion and a\n> distribution framework. You’d be able to offer Chessnut products to your\n> community, including customers we refer from the region.\n> To be clear, we’re not asking you to push sales. The idea is simply to\n> give players and visitors a way to purchase if they become interested after\n> trying the products at your events — a natural conversion, not a hard sell.\n> To make this as low-risk as possible for you, there’s no need to hold\n> inventory upfront. You can start with a pre-order model — collect a deposit\n> from customers, place orders with us weekly, and we’ll ship accordingly.\n> Once you see steady demand, we can revisit whether holding stock makes\n> sense.\n> In return, we’d ask for:\n> - Logo placement on banners, marketing materials, and event backdrops\n> - Brand visibility at tournaments and club activities throughout the year\n> - Recognition as an official Chessnut distribution partner in the region\n> - Opportunities for players and visitors to experience Chessnut products\n> firsthand at your events\n> Does this sound like something you’d be open to exploring?\n> Looking forward to your thoughts.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：Ammar sbahi\n> 发送时间：2026年7月7日(周二) 23:28\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主 题：Re: Sponsorship Opportunity - Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club\n>\n> Dear Stella,\n>\n> Thank you for your thoughtful reply and for your interest in exploring a\n> long-term collaboration with Al Ain Chess and Mind Games Club.\n>\n> Our vision is to build a long-term strategic partnership with Chessnut\n> that supports the continued growth of chess in Al Ain and across the UAE.\n>\n> We are looking for a partnership that combines both financial sponsorship\n> and product support. The financial sponsorship would help us organize\n> tournaments, youth programs, community events, marketing activities, and\n> improve the overall player experience. At the same time, we would be\n> delighted to incorporate Chessnut smart boards and other Chessnut products\n> into our tournaments, training sessions, and promotional activities.\n>\n> At this stage, we are open to discussing different sponsorship models and\n> support levels. We would be pleased to hear Chessnut's recommendations\n> regarding both financial sponsorship and product support, based on what you\n> believe would be the best fit for a long-term partnership. We are confident\n> we can develop a collaboration that delivers value for both organizations.\n>\n> In return, Chessnut would receive year-round brand exposure through:\n>\n>\n> - Logo placement on tournament banners, marketing materials, and event\n> backdrops.\n> - Recognition across our social media channels and promotional\n> campaigns.\n> - Brand visibility at tournaments and club activities throughout the\n> year.\n> - The opportunity to showcase Chessnut products during events and\n> allow players and visitors to experience them firsthand.\n> - Recognition as an official strategic partner of Al Ain Chess Club.\n>\n>\n> We believe this partnership can create meaningful value for both Chessnut\n> and the growing chess community in the UAE, and If you feel it would be\n> helpful, we would be happy to schedule an online meeting to discuss the\n> partnership further.\n>\n> Thank you once again, and I look forward to your thoughts.\n>\n> Best regards,\n>\n> On Tue, Jul 7, 2026 at 2:52 PM Stella Zhuang stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com> wrote:\n> Dear Ammar,\n>\n> Thank you for your detailed proposal — it’s a well-structured opportunity\n> and we’re genuinely interested in exploring a long-term collaboration with\n> Al Ain Chess Club.\n> Before we dive deeper, I’d like to understand how you envision this\n> partnership. For example, what kind of involvement are you looking for from\n> Chessnut? Do you have a rough scope or budget in mind?\n> This would help us better assess how we can align with your needs and put\n> together a more tailored proposal.\n> Looking forward to your thoughts.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：contact\n> 发送时间：2026年7月5日(周日) 00:40\n> 收件人：\"stella.zhuang\"\n> 主 题：Fwd: Sponsorship Opportunity - Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club\n>\n> AI routed this ticket to Stella and forwarded a copy for visibility.\n> Reason: The ticket is a sponsorship and long-term collaboration proposal\n> from a chess club, which falls under partnership/collaboration routing\n> handled by Stella.\n>\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n> On Sat, 4 Jul at 5:02 PM , Ammar sbahi wrote:\n> Dear Chessnut Team,\n>\n> I hope you are doing well.\n>\n> My name is Ammar Sbahi, Marketing & Events Coordinator at Al Ain Chess &\n> Mind Games Club.\n>\n> I am reaching out from our official club email to present a structured\n> sponsorship opportunity for a long-term collaboration between Chessnut and\n> our club.\n>\n> Al Ain Chess Club is one of the most active chess organizations in the\n> UAE, currently organizing and participating in more than 40 chess events\n> annually, including:\n>\n> - Official tournaments\n> - Community competitions\n> - Youth & school programs\n> - Collaborative chess activations across the UAE\n> - Proposed Partnership Opportunity\n>\n> We would like to explore a strategic collaboration with Chessnut that may\n> include:\n>\n> - Official sponsorship of selected tournaments and events\n> - Product showcasing and on-site activation during events\n> - Branding presence across event materials and digital coverage\n> - Integration of Chessnut products in training and competition\n> environments\n> - Long-term visibility within the UAE chess community\n>\n>\n> *Audience & Reach*\n> Our events attract a diverse chess audience, including juniors, amateurs,\n> and competitive players, with continuous engagement from schools,\n> academies, and local chess communities.\n>\n> *Collaboration Vision*\n> We are looking to build a long-term strategic partnership rather than a\n> one-time activation, where Chessnut becomes an integrated part of our\n> growing chess ecosystem in the UAE.\n>\n> We would be happy to share a detailed proposal deck, event calendar, and\n> media insights if there is interest in moving forward.\n>\n> *You can also find coverage of our latest activities and events on our\n> official Instagram page: **https://www.instagram.com/acmgae/\n> *\n> *Website:* *https://acmg.ae/ *\n>\n> Looking forward to your thoughts and the possibility of working together.\n>\n> Best regards,\n>\n> --\n> Ammar Sbahi\n> Marketing & Events Coordinator\n> *Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club*\n> Landline: +971 3 763 3387\n> Mobile: +971 56 207 1929\n> Al Ain - United Arab Emirates\n>\n>\n> 123344:2750839\n>\n>\n> --\n>\n> Ammar Sbahi\n> Marketing & Events Coordinator\n>\n> *Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club*\n>\n> Landline: +971 3 763 3387\n>\n> Mobile: +971 56 207 1929\n>\n> Al Ain - United Arab Emirates\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> --\n>\n> Ammar Sbahi\n> Marketing & Events Coordinator\n>\n> *Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club*\n>\n> Landline: +971 3 763 3387\n>\n> Mobile: +971 56 207 1929\n>\n> Al Ain - United Arab Emirates\n>\n>\n>\n\n--\n[image: Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club]\nAmmar Sbahi\nMarketing & Events Coordinator\nAl Ain Chess & Mind Games Club\nLandline: +971 3 763 3387\nMobile: +971 56 207 1929\nAl Ain, United Arab Emirates\n\nDear Stella, Thank you for the update, and no worries about the delay. The proposed framework sounds great from our side, and I believe it provides a strong foundation for a long-term partnership. We appreciate your openness and look forward to hearing from you once you&#39;ve discussed the remaining details with your team. Best regards, On Fri, Jul 17, 2026 at 1:27 PM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi Ammar, Thanks for your follow-up — and sorry for the delay on our side. This project involves quite a few details, so I&#39;ll need to discuss it with my team before I can give you a clear answer. That said, I&#39;d like to share my initial thoughts with you, so we can align expectations and move more efficiently once I come back to you. Here&#39;s what I have in mind: Products included in the sponsorship: one unit of each product in our lineup. Shipping to the UAE: Chessnut will cover the cost of sending the sponsored units to your location. Customer purchases: shipping costs for customer orders will be covered by the buyers themselves. Partnership duration: we&#39;re open to an annual partnership, which would allow us to support multiple events throughout the year. Event support: the level of material support will depend on the scale of each tournament, the number of participants, and the promotional efforts around it — we&#39;ll evaluate case by case. For the rest, I&#39;ll need to discuss internally with my team before I can confirm anything. In the meantime, I&#39;d love to hear your thoughts on this framework — especially if you have any preferences or suggestions on how we could structure this to work better for both sides. That would help us move faster once we&#39;re ready to finalize. I&#39;ll get back to you as soon as I have a clearer picture. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Ammar sbahi &lt; ammar@acmg.ae &gt; 发送时间：2026年7月15日(周三) 22:01 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Re: Sponsorship Opportunity - Al Ain Chess &amp; Mind Games Club Dear Stella, I hope you&#39;re doing well. I just wanted to follow up on my previous email regarding the potential partnership between Chessnut and Al Ain Chess Club. We remain very interested in exploring this collaboration and would appreciate any updates regarding the sponsorship details when you have the opportunity. We look forward to hearing from you and hope to move forward together soon. Thank you for your time. On Wed, Jul 8, 2026 at 12:28 PM Ammar sbahi &lt; ammar@acmg.ae &gt; wrote: Dear Stella, Thank you for your thoughtful proposal and for taking the time to outline your vision for a long-term partnership. We truly appreciate the opportunity and believe this could be the beginning of a valuable collaboration between Chessnut and Al Ain Chess Club. We are very interested in the product sponsorship model and the pre-order distribution approach, especially as it allows us to introduce Chessnut products to our community without the need to hold inventory. Before moving forward, we would appreciate a few additional details regarding: The products included in the sponsorship (models and quantities). The estimated annual value of the sponsorship. Whether shipping costs to the UAE are covered by Chessnut. The distributor margin and ordering process. Whether the partnership is intended to be annual and include support for multiple tournaments and club activities throughout the year. Once we have these details, we will be pleased to discuss the next steps and work together to establish a successful long-term partnership. We look forward to your response and are excited about the potential opportunities this partnership can create for both Chessnut and Al Ain Chess Club. Best regards, Ammar Sbahi Marketing &amp; Events Coordinator Al Ain Chess &amp; Mind Games Club Landline:  +971 3 763 3387 Mobile:   +971 56 207 1929 Al Ain -  United Arab Emirates On Wed, 8 Jul 2026 at 11:49 AM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Dear Ammar, Thanks for your detailed response — it’s clear you’ve put thought into this. On the financial sponsorship side, we’re not able to offer cash support, as Chessnut doesn’t currently have a direct sales channel in the Middle East. However, we do see a number of customers from the region reaching out to us, and they often have no easy way to purchase our products. What we’d like to propose instead is a product-based sponsorship model, combined with a distribution opportunity for your club. Here’s what we have in mind: We can provide product sponsorship — a full set of boards, tournament prizes, and ongoing event support — along with social media promotion and a distribution framework. You’d be able to offer Chessnut products to your community, including customers we refer from the region. To be clear, we’re not asking you to push sales. The idea is simply to give players and visitors a way to purchase if they become interested after trying the products at your events — a natural conversion, not a hard sell. To make this as low-risk as possible for you, there’s no need to hold inventory upfront. You can start with a pre-order model — collect a deposit from customers, place orders with us weekly, and we’ll ship accordingly. Once you see steady demand, we can revisit whether holding stock makes sense. In return, we’d ask for: - Logo placement on banners, marketing materials, and event backdrops - Brand visibility at tournaments and club activities throughout the year - Recognition as an official Chessnut distribution partner in the region - Opportunities for players and visitors to experience Chessnut products firsthand at your events Does this sound like something you’d be open to exploring? Looking forward to your thoughts. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Ammar sbahi &lt; ammar@acmg.ae &gt; 发送时间：2026年7月7日(周二) 23:28 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Re: Sponsorship Opportunity - Al Ain Chess &amp; Mind Games Club Dear Stella, Thank you for your thoughtful reply and for your interest in exploring a long-term collaboration with Al Ain Chess and Mind Games Club. Our vision is to build a long-term strategic partnership with Chessnut that supports the continued growth of chess in Al Ain and across the UAE. We are looking for a partnership that combines both financial sponsorship and product support. The financial sponsorship would help us organize tournaments, youth programs, community events, marketing activities, and improve the overall player experience. At the same time, we would be delighted to incorporate Chessnut smart boards and other Chessnut products into our tournaments, training sessions, and promotional activities. At this stage, we are open to discussing different sponsorship models and support levels. We would be pleased to hear Chessnut&#39;s recommendations regarding both financial sponsorship and product support, based on what you believe would be the best fit for a long-term partnership. We are confident we can develop a collaboration that delivers value for both organizations. In return, Chessnut would receive year-round brand exposure through: Logo placement on tournament banners, marketing materials, and event backdrops. Recognition across our social media channels and promotional campaigns. Brand visibility at tournaments and club activities throughout the year. The opportunity to showcase Chessnut products during events and allow players and visitors to experience them firsthand. Recognition as an official strategic partner of Al Ain Chess Club. We believe this partnership can create meaningful value for both Chessnut and the growing chess community in the UAE, and If you feel it would be helpful, we would be happy to schedule an online meeting to discuss the partnership further. Thank you once again, and I look forward to your thoughts. Best regards, On Tue, Jul 7, 2026 at 2:52 PM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Dear Ammar, Thank you for your detailed proposal — it’s a well-structured opportunity and we’re genuinely interested in exploring a long-term collaboration with Al Ain Chess Club. Before we dive deeper, I’d like to understand how you envision this partnership. For example, what kind of involvement are you looking for from Chessnut? Do you have a rough scope or budget in mind? This would help us better assess how we can align with your needs and put together a more tailored proposal. Looking forward to your thoughts. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：contact &lt; contact@chessnutech.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年7月5日(周日) 00:40 收件人：&quot;stella.zhuang&quot;&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Fwd: Sponsorship Opportunity - Al Ain Chess &amp; Mind Games Club\n\nAI routed this ticket to Stella and forwarded a copy for visibility.\n\nReason: The ticket is a sponsorship and long-term collaboration proposal from a chess club, which falls under partnership/collaboration routing handled by Stella. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n\nOn\n\nSat, 4 Jul at 5:02 PM\n\n, Ammar sbahi &lt; ammar@acmg.ae &gt; wrote:\n\nDear Chessnut Team, I hope you are doing well. My name is Ammar Sbahi, Marketing &amp; Events Coordinator at Al Ain Chess &amp; Mind Games Club. I am reaching out from our official club email to present a structured sponsorship opportunity for a long-term collaboration between Chessnut and our club. Al Ain Chess Club is one of the most active chess organizations in the UAE, currently organizing and participating in more than 40 chess events annually, including: Official tournaments Community competitions Youth &amp; school programs Collaborative chess activations across the UAE Proposed Partnership Opportunity We would like to explore a strategic collaboration with Chessnut that may include: Official sponsorship of selected tournaments and events Product showcasing and on-site activation during events Branding presence across event materials and digital coverage Integration of Chessnut products in training and competition environments Long-term visibility within the UAE chess community Audience &amp; Reach Our events attract a diverse chess audience, including juniors, amateurs, and competitive players, with continuous engagement from schools, academies, and local chess communities. Collaboration Vision We are looking to build a long-term strategic partnership rather than a one-time activation, where Chessnut becomes an integrated part of our growing chess ecosystem in the UAE. We would be happy to share a detailed proposal deck, event calendar, and media insights if there is interest in moving forward. You can also find coverage of our latest activities and events on our official Instagram page:  https://www.instagram.com/acmgae/ Website:   https://acmg.ae/ Looking forward to your thoughts and the possibility of working together. Best regards, -- Ammar Sbahi Marketing &amp; Events Coordinator Al Ain Chess &amp; Mind Games Club Landline:  +971 3 763 3387 Mobile:   +971 56 207 1929 Al Ain -  United Arab Emirates\n\n123344:2750839 -- Ammar Sbahi Marketing &amp; Events Coordinator Al Ain Chess &amp; Mind Games Club Landline:  +971 3 763 3387 Mobile:   +971 56 207 1929 Al Ain -  United Arab 