ad placement, and we also offer an\n> affiliate program (2% extra discount + 5% commission). That's the baseline.\n> If we find that Chessnut is a great fit for your channel, we're definitely\n> open to discussing more flexible arrangements.\n>\n> One more thing — I've recently migrated my email account. Going forward,\n> please use my new email: stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com. I've cc'd this\n> email as well.\n>\n> Looking forward to hearing your thoughts.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n> On Mon, 13 Apr at 7:11 PM , Joachim Mouhamad partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com> wrote:\n> Hi Stella,\n> Thanks for your patience — I was recently playing a tournament in Las\n> Palmas and just got back to a more normal schedule.\n> After looking into your products more carefully, I believe the most\n> natural integration for me is through the *training and preparation phase* of\n> my Road to GM journey.\n> A big part of my preparation involves playing against engines and bots.\n> Until now, I was often playing on my phone while manually reproducing the\n> moves on a physical board to stay closer to real tournament conditions —\n> which is not very practical.\n> This is where I see strong value in Chessnut — and more specifically in\n> the *Chessnut Move (it feels like the best fit for my use compared to the\n> Pro I initially had in mind)*.\n> Being able to train on a real board, with moves played automatically,\n> while staying fully immersed in tournament-like conditions is, in my view,\n> extremely valuable for players who are serious about improving.\n> *From a content perspective*, I see a natural integration within:\n>\n> - My Road To GM tournament videos : (for example, first minutes of\n> this video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AAZ1-9_FZfo )\n> - As well as my tournament preparation storytelling / vlog-style\n> content (for example first minutes of this video :\n> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OPKQNvDHc48)\n>\n> As a starting 