      "subject": "Re: Partnership Inquiry: Product Content for Chess Companion",
      "summary": "Hello Stella, Thank you for your email and your kind words. I look forward to partnering in the future. Right now, I'll be working on growing the audience and once I create a few videos, I'll send them out to you for review! Thank you so much Stella! On Tue, J",
      "body": "Hello Stella,\n\nThank you for your email and your kind words. I look forward to\npartnering in the future.\n\nRight now, I'll be working on growing the audience and once I create a few\nvideos, I'll send them out to you for review!\n\nThank you so much Stella!\n\nOn Tue, Jul 7, 2026 at 5:07 AM Stella Zhuang\nwrote:\n\n> Hi Justin,\n>\n> Thanks for reaching out — and thank you for your continued support. It\n> really means a lot to hear that our boards have become part of your chess\n> routine.\n> To be honest, the Companion is our newest product and we’re currently out\n> of stock. We’re also being quite selective with review units at this stage,\n> so I’m not able to offer one right now.\n>\n> That said, you can always create content around our existing Chessnut\n> boards. If you do, feel free to send me the link — I’ll have our Google Ads\n> team run campaigns on it to help boost your channel’s visibility. Down the\n> line, we may also be able to sponsor a product, and you’ll earn commissions\n> through the affiliate program in the meantime.\n>\n> Do you have any content plans or a timeline in mind? Let me know — happy\n> to see how we can work together.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：contact\n> 发送时间：2026年7月4日(周六) 23:11\n> 收件人：\"stella.zhuang\"\n> 主 题：Fwd: Partnership Inquiry: Product Content for Chess Companion\n>\n> Please take a look at ticket #123327\n> raised by\n> Justin Davito (justin.thechessapprentice@gmail.com).\n> Best，\n> Jony He\n> Customer Service Representative, Chessnut\n> https://chessnutech.com\n>\n>\n> On Sat, 4 Jul at 1:24 PM , Justin Davito justin.thechessapprentice@gmail.com> wrote:\n> Hi Chessnut Team,\n>\n> My name is Justin Davito, and I’ve been a fan of Chessnut since I started\n> using your boards. Your boards have become an essential part of my chess\n> routine, and I’ve been working on a project to showcase the tactile,\n> high-end experience of integrating your hardware into a serious home-study\n> environment and a tournament like experience.\n>\n> I’m reaching out because I would like to produce a long-form video review\n> of the Chessnut Companion showcasing what the Chess Companion offers to\n> Chess players, tournament competitors, and coaches.\n>\n> I specialize in high-production, cinematic media, and my goal is to create\n> a polished, deep-dive resource that helps potential buyers understand the\n> value of the Chess Companion.\n>\n> In exchange for a review unit, I will provide:\n> A high-production, deep-dive review: A professional, searchable video\n> designed to assist others in their own buying journey.\n> Asset deliverables: I will provide the edited video of the content for\n> your team to use across your own social media and marketing channels.\n> Full usage rights: You will have full permission to use the produced\n> content on your website or official brand channels.\n>\n> You can view the quality of my production work here:\n> https://youtube.com/shorts/20lq3V_Q6bA?is=HH7bVnOWAqIfv0PC\n>\n> As a genuine fan of what you’re building, I’m confident I can create a\n> piece that perfectly captures the \"Chessnut experience.\" Are you open to\n> discussing this collaboration?\n>\n> Best regards,\n> *Justin Davito*\n> 123327:2750839\n>\n>\n\nHello Stella, Thank you for your email and your kind words.   I look forward to partnering in the future.  Right now, I&#39;ll be working on growing the audience and once I create a few videos, I&#39;ll send them out to you for review!   Thank you so much Stella!   On Tue, Jul 7, 2026 at 5:07 AM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi Justin, Thanks for reaching out — and thank you for your continued support. It really means a lot to hear that our boards have become part of your chess routine. To be honest, the Companion is our newest product and we’re currently out of stock. We’re also being quite selective with review units at this stage, so I’m not able to offer one right now. That said, you can always create content around our existing Chessnut boards. If you do, feel free to send me the link — I’ll have our Google Ads team run campaigns on it to help boost your channel’s visibility. Down the line, we may also be able to sponsor a product, and you’ll earn commissions through the affiliate program in the meantime. Do you have any content plans or a timeline in mind? Let me know — happy to see how we can work together. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：contact &lt; contact@chessnutech.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年7月4日(周六) 23:11 收件人：&quot;stella.zhuang&quot;&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Fwd: Partnership Inquiry: Product Content for Chess Companion Please take a look at ticket #123327 raised by Justin Davito ( justin.thechessapprentice@gmail.com ). Best， Jony He Customer Service Representative, Chessnut https://chessnutech.com\n\nOn\nSat, 4 Jul at 1:24 PM\n, Justin Davito &lt; justin.thechessapprentice@gmail.com &gt; wrote:\n\nHi Chessnut Team, My name is Justin Davito, and I’ve been a fan of Chessnut since I started using your boards. Your boards have become an essential part of my chess routine, and I’ve been working on a project to showcase the tactile, high-end experience of integrating your hardware into a serious home-study environment and a tournament like experience . I’m reaching out because I would like to produce a long -form video review of the Chessnut Companion showcasing what the Chess Companion offers to Chess players, tournament competitors, and coaches. I specialize in high-production, cinematic media, and my goal is to create a polished, deep-dive resource that helps potential buyers understand the value of the Chess Companion. In exchange for a review unit, I will provide:   A high-production, deep-dive review: A professional, searchable video designed to assist others in their own buying journey.   Asset deliverables: I will provide the edited video of the content for your team to use across your own social media and marketing channels.   Full usage rights: You will have full permission to use the produced content on your website or official brand channels. You can view the quality of my production work here:  https://youtube.com/shorts/20lq3V_Q6bA?is=HH7bVnOWAqIfv0PC As a genuine fan of what you’re building, I’m confident I can create a piece that perfectly captures the &quot;Chessnut experience.&quot; Are you open to discussing this collaboration? Best regards, Justin Davito\n\n123327:2750839",
