      "subject": "[Chessnut Support] Business / Partnership - Chessnut Pro",
      "summary": "New support request from Chessnut website: Name: Giorgio Donnoli Email: developer@chesstools.it Order Number: N/A Inquiry Type: Business / Partnership Product: Chessnut Pro Description: Subject: ChessFlow — a new iOS training app built for Chessnut boards (lau",
      "body": "New support request from Chessnut website:\n\nName: Giorgio Donnoli\nEmail: developer@chesstools.it\nOrder Number: N/A\nInquiry Type: Business / Partnership\nProduct: Chessnut Pro\n\nDescription:\nSubject: ChessFlow — a new iOS training app built for Chessnut boards (launching September)\n\nHi Chessnut team,\n\nI&#x27;m Giorgio Donnoli, an iOS developer and active tournament chess player from Italy,\nand I&#x27;ve spent the past year building an app designed from day one around your boards.\n\nChessFlow turns a Chessnut board into an opening repertoire trainer. You play your\nprep on the real board; the app follows along with LED guidance and records every\nmove on an electronic scoresheet — the same gesture and mindset as a rated\ntournament game. Under the hood it schedules each line with spaced repetition,\nand when a training line ends you can play the position out against Stockfish\nwithout leaving the board.\n\nYou can see it here, with real photos of the app running on an Air+:\nhttps://www.chesstools.it/chessflow.html\n\nChessFlow launches on the App Store in September 2026, and it will be one of the\nfew third-party training apps that make owning a Chessnut board *more* valuable —\nevery ChessFlow user is a Chessnut customer, and the product page already tells\npeople which boards to buy.\n\nHere&#x27;s where you can help. All development so far has been on my own Chessnut\nAir+. The BLE protocol should make the app work on the Go and the Pro as well,\nbut I won&#x27;t advertise compatibility I haven&#x27;t verified on real hardware — my\nusers will be tournament players, and they notice.\n\nWould you be willing to provide one Chessnut Go and one Chessnut Pro as test\nunits? In return I&#x27;ll certify and maintain full compatibility across the range,\nlist the supported boards prominently on the site and App Store page, and link\nto your store as the place to get them. I&#x27;m also happy to share TestFlight\naccess so your team can try the app before launch, and to send structured\nfeedback on anything I find in the BLE layer along the way.\n\nI&#x27;d love to make ChessFlow the training app Chessnut owners recommend to each\nother. Shipping two boards is the cheapest marketing you&#x27;ll buy this year.\n\nBest regards,\nGiorgio Donnoli\nChessTools — https://www.chesstools.it\ndeveloper@chesstools.it\n\nVideo Link: https://www.chesstools.it/chessflow.html\n\n---\nSubmitted via Chessnut Contact Form",
      "bodyChinese": "New support request from Chessnut website:\n\nName: Giorgio Donnoli\nEmail: developer@chesstools.it\nOrder Number: N/A\nInquiry Type: Business / Partnership\nProduct: Chessnut Pro\n\nDescription:\nSubject: ChessFlow — a new iOS training app built for Chessnut boards (launching September)\n\nHi Chessnut team,\n\nI&#x27;m Giorgio Donnoli, an iOS developer and active tournament chess player from Italy,\nand I&#x27;ve spent the past year building an app designed from day one around your boards.\n\nChessFlow turns a Chessnut board into an opening repertoire trainer. You play your\nprep on the real board; the app follows along with LED guidance and records every\nmove on an electronic scoresheet — the same gesture and mindset as a rated\ntournament game. Under the hood it schedules each line with spaced repetition,\nand when a training line ends you can play the position out against Stockfish\nwithout leaving the board.\n\nYou can see it here, with real photos of the app running on an Air+:\nhttps://www.chesstools.it/chessflow.html\n\nChessFlow launches on the App Store in September 2026, and it will be one of the\nfew third-party training apps that make owning a Chessnut board *more* valuable —\nevery ChessFlow user is a Chessnut customer, and the product page already tells\npeople which boards to buy.\n\nHere&#x27;s where you can help. All development so far has been on my own Chessnut\nAir+. The BLE protocol should make the app work on the Go and the Pro as well,\nbut I won&#x27;t advertise compatibility I haven&#x27;t verified on real hardware — my\nusers will be tournament players, and they notice.\n\nWould you be willing to provide one Chessnut Go and one Chessnut Pro as test\nunits? In return I&#x27;ll certify and maintain full compatibility across the range,\nlist the supported boards prominently on the site and App Store page, and link\nto your store as the place to get them. I&#x27;m also happy to share TestFlight\naccess so your team can try the app before launch, and to send structured\nfeedback on anything I find in the BLE layer along the way.\n\nI&#x27;d love to make ChessFlow the training app Chessnut owners recommend to each\nother. Shipping two boards is the cheapest marketing you&#x27;ll buy this year.\n\nBest regards,\nGiorgio Donnoli\nChessTools — https://www.chesstools.it\ndeveloper@chesstools.it\n\nVideo Link: https://www.chesstools.it/chessflow.html\n\n---\nSubmitted via Chessnut Contact Form",
      "summaryChinese": "New support request from Chessnut website: Name: Giorgio Donnoli Email: developer@chesstools.it Order Number: N/A Inquiry Type: Business / Partnership Product: Chessnut Pro Description: Subject: ChessFlow — a new iOS training app built for Chessnut boards (lau",
