appy to discuss\n> what that could look like.\n> Let us know your thoughts. We're excited about the possibility of working\n> together over the long run!\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：Elena Kotrikadze\n> 发送时间：2026年6月24日(周三) 05:51\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主 题：Re: Collaboration Invitation – Chessnut × Twitch Creator\n>\n> Hey Stella!\n>\n> I was wondering if there’s an update on collaboration with you guys? Would\n> love to explore what that would look like and excited for the opportunity\n> since the boards look so advanced!\n>\n> Looking forward to hearing from you,\n>\n> Lena.\n>\n> On Thu, May 21, 2026 at 21:31 Elena Kotrikadze\n> wrote:\n>\n> Hey Stella,\n>\n> Thanks for the offer on the board, I'd love to have it on stream! If\n> you're interested in more, I also do dedicated sponsored streams ($400) and\n> reels posted across all my platforms ($400). I've worked with Leap in a\n> similar setup so I know how to make it land well.\n>\n> Analytics attached for the last 30 days for my Instagram and Tiktok.\n>\n> Let me know what you think,\n>\n> Lena.\n>\n>\n>\n> On Mon, May 18, 2026 at 5:51 PM Stella Zhuang stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com> wrote:\n> Hi Elena,\n>\n> I'm Stella, Business Development Manager at Chessnut.\n>\n> We make smart chessboards that connect to Chess.com and Lichess – letting\n> you play online opponents on a real physical board while streaming. It\n> looks great on stream.\n>\n> You can check out our products here:\n> 🔗 https://www.chessnutech.com/pages/chessnut-air-plus\n>\n> Here's what I'd like to offer you:\n>\n> A free Chessnut Air+ (wooden smart chessboard) – just place it on your\n> desk during streams. No need to talk about it unless you want to.\n> Optional: An affiliate program – earn commissions when your viewers\n> purchase using your unique link.\n> Optional: If you have a rate for sponsored content, feel free to share it.\n> We're open to discussing paid collaboration as well.\n>\n> No pressure. No complicated contracts. Just a board that looks good on\n> stream.\n>\n> If you're interested, let me know. I'm happy to share more details.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n>\n\nHey Stella! Would you mind describing what content exactly would Chessnut like to see me do on streams? Or is it just play and analyze type of stream? And what board would I be using?  And it’s 4 streams per month or per 3 month period?  Thank you! On Tue, Jul 7, 2026 at 14:58 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi Lena, We’re open to testing this with a fixed rate of $500 per month for the first 3 months (covering 4 streams), with the affiliate commission on top. If things go well, we can revisit the rate afterward. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Elena Kotrikadze &lt; elena.kotrikadze@gmail.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年7月5日(周日) 06:05 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Re: Collaboration Invitation – Chessnut × Twitch Creator Hi Stella, Thanks for the detail, I like the affiliate structure and I’m happy to have that as part of the deal. But I don’t see a fixed fee mentioned for the streams themselves. That’s the piece that matters most to me, the affiliate commission can sit on top as a bonus, not replace it. Could you share what you’re able to offer as a fixed rate for the 4 streams a month? Best, Lena On Tue, Jun 30, 2026 at 11:09 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi Lena, Thanks for your message. We’d love to explore a long‑term partnership with you. To be honest, this would be our first fixed collaboration using live streams as the main format, so we don’t have a set budget yet. We’re open to discussing what feels fair — probably something modest to start, and we can adjust as we go. In terms of content, we’d be looking at around 1 live stream per week (about 4 streams a month), plus a Chessnut link in your bio (your own affiliate link, so purchases count toward your commission). You’ll also get a discount code that’s 2% higher than our site rate, and a tiered commission starting at 5%, going up to 10% as sales grow. We already have creators earning over $5,000 a year through our affiliate program, and the number keeps growing. If the collaboration goes well, we’d be happy to tag you as an official Chessnut partner on Instagram and support your streams regularly — not automatic, but something we’d actively move toward if we see a good fit. On the Shenzhen office question — yes, our office is there, but live streaming is still a relatively new area for us, so I don’t have a clear answer at this stage. Maybe in the future. We see this as a real partnership, not a one‑off transaction — something we’d like to build together over time. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Elena Kotrikadze &lt; elena.kotrikadze@gmail.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年6月26日(周五) 19:38 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Re: Collaboration Invitation – Chessnut × Twitch Creator Hey Stella, I appreciate your honesty and I would absolutely prefer a long term partnership! Let me know what retainer would look like, how many streams/reels a month you looking for?  On a separate note, I am relocation to Shenzhen beginning of next year and I just saw Rachel did a tour of Chessnut’s office there, I was wondering if there’s any opportunities for creators in China? No worries if not, just thought I’d ask. Looking forward hearing from you, Lena. On Wed, Jun 24, 2026 at 14:57 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi Lena, Thanks for your follow-up, and thank you for your interest in Chessnut and your kind words about our boards! Just to be upfront, we&#39;re more interested in building a longer‑term partnership rather than a one‑off project. We&#39;d love to explore something that works on an ongoing basis, like regular integration in your streams or content, rather than a single sponsored post or video. If that sounds like something you&#39;d be open to, we&#39;d be happy to discuss what that could look like. Let us know your thoughts. We&#39;re excited about the possibility of working together over the long run! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Elena Kotrikadze &lt; elena.kotrikadze@gmail.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年6月24日(周三) 05:51 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Re: Collaboration Invitation – Chessnut × Twitch Creator Hey Stella!  I was wondering if there’s an update on collaboration with you guys? Would love to explore what that would look like and excited for the opportunity since the boards look so advanced! Looking forward to hearing from you, Lena. On Thu, May 21, 2026 at 21:31 Elena Kotrikadze &lt; elena.kotrikadze@gmail.com &gt; wrote: Hey Stella, Thanks for the offer on the board, I&#39;d love to have it on stream! If you&#39;re interested in more, I also do dedicated sponsored streams ($400) and reels posted across all my platforms ($400). I&#39;ve worked with Leap in a similar setup so I know how to make it land well.  Analytics attached for the last 30 days for my Instagram and Tiktok. Let me know what you think, Lena. On Mon, May 18, 2026 at 5:51 PM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi Elena , I&#39;m Stella, Business Development Manager at Chessnut. We make smart chessboards that connect to Chess.com and Lichess – letting you play online opponents on a real physical board while streaming. It looks great on stream. You can check out our products here: 🔗 https://www.chessnutech.com/pages/chessnut-air-plus Here&#39;s what I&#39;d like to offer you: A free Chessnut Air+ (wooden smart chessboard) – just place it on your desk during streams. No need to talk about it unless you want to. Optional: An affiliate program – earn commissions when your viewers purchase using your unique link. Optional: If you have a rate for sponsored content, feel free to share it. We&#39;re open to discussing paid collaboration as well. No pressure. No complicated contracts. Just a board that looks good on stream. If you&#39;re interested, let me know. I&#39;m happy to share more details. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut",
