      "body": "Hi Stella,\nGood news, thanks. Here are the details for shipping:\nRyan Fenwick\n07880 059244\n28 Blackthorn Drive, Hurworth, DL2 2FU, United Kingdom\nOn the Tax ID: I don't have one to give for a personal press shipment, so I'd suggest declaring it as a review sample or gift at low value, which normally clears UK customs without one. If your logistics team needs anything specific from my end to make that work, tell me what and I'll sort it.\nOn timing, send it as soon as you can and we'll be fine. My hard copy deadline is 14th August, so as long as it reaches me a week or so before that, I've got time to give it a proper run. If shipping looks like it'll be tight, let me know the tracking once it's on its way, and I can plan around it.\nBest,\nRyan\n\nRyan Fenwick\nSales Director\nNewsquest Media Group | LOCALiQ\n\n07880 059244\n\nnewsquest.co.uk | localiq.co.uk\n\n[cid:a8644331-c45a-455d-be93-c1a9dc609b66]\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Stella Zhuang\nSent: Tuesday, July 07, 2026 10:39 AM\nTo: Ryan Fenwick\nSubject: 回复：Re: BUSINESSiQ September 2026 — Chessnut Move Editorial Review Request\n\nYou don't often get email from stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com. Learn why this is important\nHi Ryan,\n\nThanks for reaching out — we’d be happy to provide a review unit. However, I’m not sure if it will arrive in time for your deadline, given the shipping time required.\nTo move forward, could you please provide the following details so we can arrange the shipment?\n- Full name\n- Phone number\n- Shipping address\n- Postal code\n- Tax ID\nWe’ll do our best to get it to you as soon as possible.\n\nBest,\nStella\nBusiness Development Manager | Chessnut\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\n发件人：contact\n发送时间：2026年7月1日(周三) 14:11\n收件人：\"stella.zhuang\"\n主　题：Fwd: Re: BUSINESSiQ September 2026 — Chessnut Move Editorial Review Request\n\n请查看由Ryan Fenwick（ryan.fenwick@localiq.co.uk）提出的工单#122480 。\n此致，\n何强\nChessnut客户服务代表\nhttps://chessnutech.com\n\nOn Tue, 30 Jun at 9:49 PM , Ryan Fenwick wrote:\nHi,\nFollowing up on my note about featuring the Chessnut Move in the September edition of BUSINESSiQ. The slot is still open and I'd like to include it.\nWith our copy deadline of 14th August approaching, I'd need a review unit in hand a couple of weeks before to give it a proper run. If it's easier, a quick yes or no on availability is all I need at this stage and I can work around the rest.\nIn case it's useful again, a recent edition of the column is here: https://edition.pagesuite.com/html5/reader/production/default.aspx?pnum=154&edid=fe229502-f8ea-4df5-a8a3-9757cda8b488&isshared=true\nBest,\nRyan Fenwick\n\nRyan Fenwick\nSales Director\nNewsquest Media Group | LOCALiQ\n\n07880 059244\n\nnewsquest.co.uk | localiq.co.uk\n\n[https://outlook.office.com/mail/inbox/id/AAkALgAAAAAAHYQDEapmEc2byACqAC%2FEWg0AoM6bGzheCUWtEec3TOKdfwANF4%2Br4QAA?nativeVersion=1.2026.623.400]\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Ryan Fenwick\nSent: Thursday, June 11, 2026 11:14 AM\nTo: contact@chessnutech.com\nSubject: BUSINESSiQ September 2026 — Chessnut Move Editorial Review Request\n\nHi,\nI'm Ryan Fenwick, tech columnist for BUSINESSiQ, the North East England quarterly business magazine. I'm building the tech section for our September 2026 edition and I'd like to consider the Chessnut Move for editorial inclusion.\nBUSINESSiQ reaches 5,000 copies per quarter — 71% of our readership are senior managers and directors. The intersection of technology and focus is a theme that runs through our tech coverage, and the Chessnut Move is a product I'd like to put in front of that audience properly.\nIf it helps to see what the coverage looks like, a recent edition of the column is available to read online — take a look here .\nIf you can provide a review unit along with any press materials and high-resolution imagery, please get in touch.\nKind regards,\nRyan\n\nRyan Fenwick\nSales Director\nNewsquest Media Group | LOCA