      "summary": "Good afternoon Stella, Please find attached the breakdown of my travel expenses for reimbursement from the recent trip. For clarity, as we generally operate in USD and the expenses were incurred across multiple foreign currencies, I have included the final rei",
      "body": "Good afternoon Stella,\n\nPlease find attached the breakdown of my travel expenses for reimbursement\nfrom the recent trip.\n\nFor clarity, as we generally operate in USD and the expenses were incurred\nacross multiple foreign currencies, I have included the final reimbursement\ntotal in USD to avoid any confusion. The USD figure below has been\nconverted using the current exchange rate of approximately *1 AUD = 0.6938\nUSD*.\n\n*Travel Costs*\n\n-\n\nSydney → Taiwan: AUD $1,392.89\n-\n\nTaiwan → Hong Kong: AUD $400.44\n-\n\nThailand → Sydney: AUD $675.00 *(I had originally booked a Hong Kong →\nSydney flight. However, after changing my travel plans, I was able to\nobtain a refund and rebook my return from Thailand at a lower cost.)*\n-\n\nAirport Transfer: AUD $92.00\n-\n\nAirport Transfer: AUD $100.00\n\nTotal (AUD): $2,660.33\n*Total (USD): $1,845.20*\n\nRegarding meal reimbursements, as a Hong Kong meal allowance was provided\nin advance and a number of meals were supplied throughout the trip, I don't\nbelieve it is necessary to go through my receipts to determine whether I\nincurred any additional eligible meal expenses. As such, I won't be\nclaiming any meal reimbursement for this trip.\n\nPlease find the relevant travel receipts attached.\n\nI'd also like to take this opportunity to thank you and the entire Chessnut\nteam for being such wonderful hosts throughout my travels. I really\nappreciate all of the support and hospitality, and it made the trip an\nenjoyable and memorable experience.\n\nKind regards,\nWade\n\nGood afternoon Stella, Please find attached the breakdown of my travel expenses for reimbursement from the recent trip. For clarity, as we generally operate in USD and the expenses were incurred across multiple foreign currencies, I have included the final reimbursement total in USD to avoid any confusion. The USD figure below has been converted using the current exchange rate of approximately 1 AUD = 0.6938 USD . Travel Costs Sydney → Taiwan: AUD $1,392.89 Taiwan → Hong Kong: AUD $400.44 Thailand → Sydney: AUD $675.00 (I had originally booked a Hong Kong → Sydney flight. However, after changing my travel plans, I was able to obtain a refund and rebook my return from Thailand at a lower cost.) Airport Transfer: AUD $92.00 Airport Transfer: AUD $100.00 Total (AUD): $2,660.33 Total (USD): $1,845.20 Regarding meal reimbursements, as a Hong Kong meal allowance was provided in advance and a number of meals were supplied throughout the trip, I don&#39;t believe it is necessary to go through my receipts to determine whether I incurred any additional eligible meal expenses. As such, I won&#39;t be claiming any meal reimbursement for this trip.\n\nPlease find the relevant travel receipts attached. I&#39;d also like to take this opportunity to thank you and the entire Chessnut team for being such wonderful hosts throughout my travels. I really appreciate all of the support and hospitality, and it made the trip an enjoyable and memorable experience.   Kind regards, W ade\n\n%PDF-1.4\n%����\n3 0 obj\n>stream\nx���l\u0014E\u0014�����A)w\u0007V��_RhK�E.@�\u001f��\u0016\n��\u000f�P!`��(?4\u0010#D�\u0010�\u0000b�b�҈�\u0018��J�\u0018\u0002�D\u0010\n����Z0R@#j)\u0005�;�|�;{���-(�4����>�}3o\u0006����}\u001b�g��!\u0000��>\u001d�Q�øὌ�a&\"��޼�,��x����@�\u001f4 � 3p��cٙ���|4��zA�`(�\u001b\u0017\bf\u001d\u0014Ww�7 �RK�e�O5}X>\u0017�ư�ze��M�\u001b,ۼ�\u0010/���[vgXÖ~�����$C;Z��/��/^�WE)F�1�)��%�h\u0015N�\n�H1�a.\u0016|�\u0018ϻ+� �\u000e��e�T����#�4���\u0004_dX-,S�E����2�\u0005�\u0010��$\f�������C�2��ϵ��;O����\"�Z�\"*�|���\bqT���|�E�6�؅�J\u0007->~�\\� vq\u001a�5dES�6:/^�\u0004\u0004C��0}\u0014ؑ�it�\"�\u000bģ��f�5Y%��'\n\u00195��2^\u0018\u0006\b�.�>O�D�M�\u0015����\u0002aX�\fϣ�2Y&U��,�B ��\u001f\u0012 (?\u0005�Q%���\u0001�\u0002� ���\u0011h�CQ\"�a�w\u000bߖ�����\u0003 \u0010�\u0019�A����m��ҭ���\u0004J6�z\u0018A���P��\u001bt��`\u000b;@{l�ذ��[\u0013\n�l�s\u001a\no��׫\u0012E�zĻ4h�Ֆ�\u0017\u0005���\u001b���:l\u001b\u00