ys welcome. We’re also open to co‑tagging on Instagram when the content goes live. Let me know if this works for you, and we can move forward with the shipping details. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl &lt;krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月26日(周五) 15:49 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主　题：回复：Odp: 回复：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series Alternatively, we could also propose another option for the prize distribution: We could award 2 boards to the players (one for the final Grand Prix winner and one for the raffle), and the 3rd board could be shipped directly to the creator, Marianczello. This way, he will have the product on hand to record dedicated content and reviews about your brand. Please let me know which of these options works best for you!\n\nDnia 26 czerwca 2026 08:32\nStella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; napisał(a):\n\nHi Krzysztof, Thanks for the detailed response — this is very helpful. On co-created content: I was thinking we could tag each other when posting Shorts or Reels, so Chessnut’s 60K followers can also discover the tournament. I think that could be a nice boost for visibility on your side too. Also, it might be helpful to feature the prize boards briefly in Marianczello’s video — showing the actual products could make them more appealing to players. The Move is quite popular right now, so that could generate some extra interest. Before we confirm the prize commitment, I have a couple of questions: - Are there other brand sponsors involved in the series besides Chessnut? If so, could you share who they are? - How will the 3 Chessnut boards be used across the 10 tournaments? Will they be awarded at the final Grand Prix standings, or distributed across individual events? - If there are other sponsors, will the Chessnut boards be presented as standalone prizes, or grouped together with oth