nut. Would something like this be possible on your side?\n> Even partial support, for example covering the flight or the hotel, could\n> already make it feasible for me to attend.\n>\n> And if it's not possible, please let me know as well so I can look for\n> another solution and plan accordingly.\n>\n> Best, Tim\n>\n>\n\nHi Stella, Thank you so much for your kind and motivating message. It really means a lot to me, and I&#39;m very happy to hear that you&#39;ve been following my progress closely! I am really happy with how the Tiktok and Instagram accounts are growing. No worries at all regarding the tournament sponsorship. I just wanted to be sure so that I could plan accordingly. Regarding the agreement, yes, I can definitely commit to at least one piece of content per day during the summer break. There may be a few rare occasions where I can&#39;t post because of an important emergency, but overall I&#39;m happy with this goal. In fact, knowing that there are people supporting me and following my journey also helps me stay consistent. I can also confirm that the address and all the information are correct. Thank you again! I&#39;m really looking forward to trying the chess clock. If I make a video about it, should I send you the link so you can promote it as before?  Also can you explain to me how I can do a collaboration post with Chessnut on instagram like you did with Swapnil, Rachel, etc? I would like to do more posts like this to reach more people showcasing the boards but I&#39;m not sure how to do it. And I&#39;m not sure if you saw my WhatsApp message, but I was wondering if it would be possible to get access to the photos from the tournament—both the pictures of us with the Chessnut boards and the photos taken during the games. I&#39;d love to use some of them for profile pictures and social media posts. I also wanted to ask if you happen to have a more basic Chessnut T-shirt available, maybe with just a small logo on it. If so, I&#39;d love one! Thank you again for all your support! Best, Tim Le mar. 30 juin 2026 à 08:05, Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; a écrit : Hi Tim, I’m really happy to see the great results you’re getting — I’m truly proud of you. I may reply slowly, but I’m still following your progress closely. Regarding the tournament sponsorship, as I mentioned before, it’s currently outside our scope since we’re focusing on working with organizers. However, the good news is that I’ve already secured approval for the DJI Pocket 3 reimbursement.  The agreement is: for the next 3 months of summer break, you’ll publish at least one piece of content per day (including long-form videos, vertical Shorts, and community posts), and at least one long-form video per week. Could you also confirm if the following address is correct? I’m about to send you 3 pieces of apparel and the chess clock. Name: Letoret Tim Phone number: +32 474767016 Street: Rue de Nalinnes 65 City: Jamioulx Postal code: 6120 Belgium Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Teltimat &lt; teltimat@gmail.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年6月30日(周二) 03:13 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Content with Chessnut Board Hi Stella, it is Tim,  I hope you&#39;re all doing well!  Since I came back from Hong Kong, I&#39;ve started posting 1–2 short videos per day featuring the Chessnut board, and the audience has been very receptive.  Many people are asking in the comments whether I&#39;m satisfied with the board, if it&#39;s worth the price, and other questions about my experience.  I&#39;ve also noticed a significant increase in sales through my affiliate code, with more than $8,500 in sales generated since I started this content strategy.  I also wanted to share this video ( https://youtu.be/RYZlPBa5ABc ) with you because it&#39;s the kind of content I was talking about regarding the possibility of playing in the European Championship in Montenegro (9 videos).  Of course, the videos would be more focused on the board itself, with commentary about the games and camera angles better suited to showcase the board.  I think this type of content could work really well and bring even more visibility to Chessnut. Would something like this be possible on your side?  Even partial support, for example covering the flight or the hotel, could already make it feasible for me to attend.  And if it&#39;s not possible, please let me know as well so I can look for another solution and plan accordingly. Best, Tim",
