      "body": "Hi Stella, it is Tim,\nI hope you're all doing well!\n\nSince I came back from Hong Kong, I've started posting 1–2 short videos per\nday featuring the Chessnut board, and the audience has been very receptive.\nMany people are asking in the comments whether I'm satisfied with the\nboard, if it's worth the price, and other questions about my experience.\n\nI've also noticed a significant increase in sales through my affiliate\ncode, with more than $8,500 in sales generated since I started this content\nstrategy.\nI also wanted to share this video (https://youtu.be/RYZlPBa5ABc) with you\nbecause it's the kind of content I was talking about regarding the\npossibility of playing in the European Championship in Montenegro (9\nvideos).\nOf course, the videos would be more focused on the board itself, with\ncommentary about the games and camera angles better suited to showcase the\nboard.\nI think this type of content could work really well and bring even more\nvisibility to Chessnut. Would something like this be possible on your side?\nEven partial support, for example covering the flight or the hotel, could\nalready make it feasible for me to attend.\n\nAnd if it's not possible, please let me know as well so I can look for\nanother solution and plan accordingly.\n\nBest, Tim\n\nHi Stella, it is Tim,  I hope you&#39;re all doing well!  Since I came back from Hong Kong, I&#39;ve started posting 1–2 short videos per day featuring the Chessnut board, and the audience has been very receptive.  Many people are asking in the comments whether I&#39;m satisfied with the board, if it&#39;s worth the price, and other questions about my experience.  I&#39;ve also noticed a significant increase in sales through my affiliate code, with more than $8,500 in sales generated since I started this content strategy.  I also wanted to share this video ( https://youtu.be/RYZlPBa5ABc ) with you because it&#39;s the kind of content I was talking about regarding the possibility of playing in the European Championship in Montenegro (9 videos).  Of course, the videos would be more focused on the board itself, with commentary about the games and camera angles better suited to showcase the board.  I think this type of content could work really well and bring even more visibility to Chessnut. Would something like this be possible on your side?  Even partial support, for example covering the flight or the hotel, could already make it feasible for me to attend.  And if it&#39;s not possible, please let me know as well so I can look for another solution and plan accordingly. Best, Tim",
      "bodyChinese": "Hi Stella, it is Tim,\nI hope you're all doing well!\n\nSince I came back from Hong Kong, I've started posting 1–2 short videos per\nday featuring the Chessnut board, and the audience has been very receptive.\nMany people are asking in the comments whether I'm satisfied with the\nboard, if it's worth the price, and other questions about my experience.\n\nI've also noticed a significant increase in sales through my affiliate\ncode, with more than $8,500 in sales generated since I started this content\nstrategy.\nI also wanted to share this video (https://youtu.be/RYZlPBa5ABc) with you\nbecause it's the kind of content I was talking about regarding the\npossibility of playing in the European Championship in Montenegro (9\nvideos).\nOf course, the videos would be more focused on the board itself, with\ncommentary about the games and camera angles better suited to showcase the\nboard.\nI think this type of content could work really well and bring even more\nvisibility to Chessnut. Would something like this be possible on your side?\nEven partial support, for example covering the flight or the hotel, could\nalready make it feasible for me to attend.\n\nAnd if it's not possible, please let me know as well so I can look for\nanother solution and plan accordingly.\n\nBest, Tim\n\nHi Stella, it is Tim,  I hope you&#39;re all doing well!  Since I came back from Hong Kong, I&#39;ve started posting 1–2 short videos per day featuring the Chessnut board, and the audience has been very receptive.  Many people are asking in the comments whether I&#39;m satisfied with the board, if it&#39;s worth the price, and other questions about my experience.  I&#39;ve also noticed a significant increase in sales through my affiliate code, with more than $8,500 in sales generated since I started this content strategy.  I also wanted to share this video ( https://youtu.be/RYZlPBa5ABc ) with you because it&#39;s the kind of content I was talking about regarding the possibili