      "body": "Hi Stella,\n\nMy sincerest apologies for the delayed response. I had actually written\nthis email before leaving for my trip on June 14th and thought I had sent\nit, but I just realized it was still sitting in my drafts and had not gone\nthrough. I’m very sorry about that.\n\nIt has also been an incredibly hectic couple of weeks as we prepare for our\nsummer camps, and I was out of the country until recently, so I’m just\ncatching up on everything now.\n\nFor now, here is the board information:\n\nModel number: CM100\nSerial number: CMB6300533\nCharging port model number: CHGCM1\n\nIn terms of the pieces affected, it is a little difficult to identify each\nspecific piece, but I would say at least half of the pieces seem to be\naffected.\n\nI also wanted to mention that we have already begun putting out some basic\nintroduction videos about the Chessnut Move unit, and we also incorporated\nit into our May 24th chess event, which was a huge success. Many parents\nshowed a lot of interest in the unit, and it was definitely something that\ncaught people’s attention.\n\nThat said, I have held off on creating a full review of the Chessnut Move\nfor the time being until we can hopefully resolve the issue. I’m very\ngrateful that Chessnut provided the unit, and there are many wonderful\nfeatures that I would be excited to highlight properly. At the same time, I\nwant to make sure that any review I share is fair, honest, and genuinely\nuseful for the families and chess players who follow us.\n\nI think it is important that I speak accurately about the full experience,\nincluding both the strengths of the unit and any practical notes around\nsetup, troubleshooting, or things that may still need to be addressed.\n\nAlso, for the videos we have shared so far, we did tag Chessnut. I just\nwanted to ask whether you received our collaboration requests for those\nvideos. Going forward, when we feature the Chessnut Move unit, do you\nprefer that we simply tag Chessnut, or would you prefer that we send\ncollaboration requests and post them as collab videos when appropriate?\n\nI’ll do my best to send the short video once I’m able to properly test and\nrecord the issue.\n\nThank you again for your help, and sorry again for the delayed response.\nArash Shahi \"Mr. S\"\nExecutive Director\nCHESS WITH MR. S INC.\n\nwww.chesswithmrs.com\nMobile: 416.456.1599\ninfo@chesswithmrs.com\nshahiarash.s@gmail.com\n\nOn Wed, May 27, 2026 at 5:04 AM Stella Zhuang\nwrote:\n\n> Hi Arash,\n>\n> Sorry for the delayed response. Could you please share your board's serial\n> number, a short video of the issue, and how many pieces are affected? I\n> will have my colleague Gwen get back to you shortly.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：Arash Shahi\n> 发送时间：2026年5月23日(周六) 07:40\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主 题：Re: Collaboration Opportunity – Chessnut Move Feature\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> I hope you’re doing very well.\n>\n> First and foremost, thank you once again to you and the Chessnut team for\n> the incredibly generous gift of the Chessnut Move unit. I truly appreciate\n> it.\n>\n> As you know, we have our Spring Checkmate Festival this Sunday, May 24th,\n> with 120 registered chess players plus their families attending, and we’ll\n> be proudly showcasing the Chessnut Move unit as part of the event\n> experience.\n>\n> I also plan to begin creating some content sharing my experience with the\n> product and my broader thoughts on it, as I genuinely think the technology\n> is incredibly impressive. Quite honestly, if someone didn’t know better, it\n> almost feels magical seeing it in action.\n>\n> That said, I wanted to reach out because I seem to be experiencing an\n> issue that appears to be similar to something other Chessnut Move owners\n> have reported.\n>\n> After fully charging the board and pieces, when everything is powered down\n> completely (board turned off, app closed, and everything fully\n> disconnected), some of the pieces continue to twitch or make tiny\n> unintended movements while resting on the board.\n>\n> I did a little digging online and it seems others may have encountered\n> similar behaviour, so I wanted to ask whether this is a known issue and\n> whether there’s a recommended fix, firmware update, reset procedure, or\n> best practice to resolve it.\n>\n> This likely won’t impact our tournament demo on Sunday, so there’s no\n> emergency—but I’d really like to understand what’s happening.\n>\n> As I begin sharing my thoughts on the product and potentially recommending\n> it to our broader chess community of students, families, and chess\n> enthusiasts, I’d love to be able to confidently explain whether this\n> behaviour is expected, avoidable, or fixable.\n>\n> Because truthfully, I think this is a remarkable product with real appeal\n> for chess-loving families and adult enthusiasts alike.\n>\n> If helpful, I’d also be happy to send along a short video of the twitching\n> behaviour.\n>\n> Thanks again for all of your kindness and support—I’d really appreciate\n> any guidance from you or your technical team.\n>\n> Warmly,\n> Arash Shahi \"Mr. S\"\n> Executive Director\n> CHESS WITH MR. S INC.\n>\n> www.chesswithmrs.com\n> Mobile: 416.456.1599\n> info@chesswithmrs.com\n> shahiarash.s@gmail.com\n>\n>\n> On Fri, May 8, 2026 at 3:42 AM Stella Zhuang stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com> wrote:\n> Hi Arash,\n>\n> That should be it. The tracking number has been updated:\n> 1ZB87K330420800754. Carrier: UPS. You should receive it soon.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：Arash Shahi\n> 发送时间：2026年4月30日(周四) 23:44\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主 题：Re: Collaboration Opportunity – Chessnut Move Feature\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> I hope you’re doing well, and my apologies for the slow response.\n>\n> We’re very 