 regards, Arash Shahi &quot;Mr. S&quot; Executive Director CHESS WITH MR. S INC. www.chesswithmrs.com Mobile: 416.456.1599 info@chesswithmrs.com shahiarash.s@gmail.com On Tue, Apr 14, 2026 at 4:05 AM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi Arash, Interested. We can provide: one Move unit (loan), remote training, discount codes, and cross-promotion. In return, we need: someone to run the demo, photos/videos, and a brief recap. Just to confirm, does the Move unit need to be returned after the event? Also, will parents be at the event? Let me know on both. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：contact &lt; contact@chessnutech.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年4月11日(周六) 15:25 收件人：&quot;stella.zhuang&quot;&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Fwd: Collaboration Opportunity – Chessnut Move Feature Please take a look at ticket #109113 raised by Arash Shahi ( info@chesswithmrs.com ). Best， Jony He Customer Service Representative, Chessnut https://chessnutech.com\n\nOn\nFri, 10 Apr at 11:51 PM\n, Arash Shahi &lt; info@chesswithmrs.com &gt; wrote:\n\nDear Chessnut Team, I hope you’re doing well. My name is Arash Shahi, and I’m the Executive Director of Chess with Mr. S., a growing chess education program based in Ontario, Canada. Each week, we work with several hundred students through our public and private school programs, in-person and online classes, weekend sessions, summer camps, and regularly hosted tournaments. Our students and families are always excited by innovative chess tools, and the Chessnut Move is something that immediately stood out to me as both engaging and highly relevant to our community. We are currently building our presence across Instagram and TikTok, with a focus on engaging, relatable, and educational chess content. Here are a couple of recent examples: Instagram: instagram.com/chess.with.mr.s.official/reel/DVgrh_HlgQ8/ TikTok: https://www.tiktok.com/@chess.with.mr.s/video/7624214657078775047 Our focus is always on creating authentic, experience-based content that genuinely resonates with our students and families, and we believe the Chessnut Move would be an exciting and natural fit within our programs. In addition, we host large-scale chess tournaments throughout the year, each reaching full capacity at 120 players, along with many attending family members and spectators. Our upcoming event, the CWMS Spring Checkmate Festival , will be held on May 24th. As part of this, we would be excited to showcase the Chessnut Move in a dedicated station at the event—giving students and families the opportunity to experience the board firsthand in a fun, interactive setting. I believe this would be a great way to introduce your product directly to a highly engaged and relevant audience. If this is something you’d be open to, I would be happy to create and share content across our platforms in addition to featuring the board at our event. I’d also be glad to discuss any specific goals or features you’d like highlighted to best support your brand. Thank you very much for your time and consideration—I’d love to explore this further. Warm regards,\nArash Shahi\nExecutive Director\nChess with Mr. S Inc. www.chesswithmrs.com\nMobile: 416.456.1599 info@chesswithmrs.com P.S. Our Spring Checkmate Festival on May 24th is approaching quickly, so if this is something you’d like to explore, I’d be happy to coordinate timing to feature the Chessnut Move at the event.\n\n109113:2750839",
