 unit, do you prefer that we simply tag Chessnut, or would you prefer that we send collaboration requests and post them as collab videos when appropriate? I’ll do my best to send the short video once I’m able to properly test and record the issue. Thank you again for your help, and sorry again for the delayed response. Arash Shahi &quot;Mr. S&quot; Executive Director CHESS WITH MR. S INC. www.chesswithmrs.com Mobile: 416.456.1599 info@chesswithmrs.com shahiarash.s@gmail.com On Wed, May 27, 2026 at 5:04 AM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi Arash, Sorry for the delayed response. Could you please share your board&#39;s serial number, a short video of the issue, and how many pieces are affected? I will have my colleague Gwen get back to you shortly. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Arash Shahi &lt; info@chesswithmrs.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年5月23日(周六) 07:40 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Re: Collaboration Opportunity – Chessnut Move Feature Hi Stella, I hope you’re doing very well. First and foremost, thank you once again to you and the Chessnut team for the incredibly generous gift of the Chessnut Move unit. I truly appreciate it. As you know, we have our Spring Checkmate Festival this Sunday, May 24th, with 120 registered chess players plus their families attending, and we’ll be proudly showcasing the Chessnut Move unit as part of the event experience. I also plan to begin creating some content sharing my experience with the product and my broader thoughts on it, as I genuinely think the technology is incredibly impressive. Quite honestly, if someone didn’t know better, it almost feels magical seeing it in action. That said, I wanted to reach out because I seem to be experiencing an issue that appears to be similar to something other Chessnut Move owners have reported. After fully charging the board and pieces, when everything is powered down completely (board turned off, app closed, and everything fully disconnected), some of the pieces continue to twitch or make tiny unintended movements while resting on the board. I did a little digging online and it seems others may have encountered similar behaviour, so I wanted to ask whether this is a known issue and whether there’s a recommended fix, firmware update, reset procedure, or best practice to resolve it. This likely won’t impact our tournament demo on Sunday, so there’s no emergency—but I’d really like to understand what’s happening. As I begin sharing my thoughts on the product and potentially recommending it to our broader chess community of students, families, and chess enthusiasts, I’d love to be able to confidently explain whether this behaviour is expected, avoidable, or fixable. Because truthfully, I think this is a remarkable product with real appeal for chess-loving families and adult enthusiasts alike. If helpful, I’d also be happy to send along a short video of the twitching behaviour. Thanks again for all of your kindness and support—I’d really appreciate any guidance from you or your technical team. Warmly, Arash Shahi &quot;Mr. S&quot; Executive Director CHESS WITH MR. S INC. www.chesswithmrs.com Mobile: 416.456.1599 info@chesswithmrs.com shahiarash.s@gmail.com On Fri, May 8, 2026 at 3:42 AM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi  Arash, That should be it. The tracking number has been updated: 1ZB87K330420800754. Carrier: UPS. You should receive it soon. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Arash Shahi &lt; info@chesswithmrs.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年4月30日(周四) 23:44 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主　题：Re: Collaboration Opportunity – Chessnut Move Feature Hi Stella, I hope you’re doing well, and my apologies for the slow response. We’re very excited to get started with this collaboration. I’ve g