      "summary": "Hi, Stella, Yes, I've received the companion. It's very cool. I've posted a couple of videos already (links below) and will use the guidance you just provided for future videos. Seems like a great device, very high quality. I noticed that it requires a little ",
      "body": "Hi, Stella,\n\nYes, I've received the companion. It's very cool. I've posted a couple of\nvideos already (links below) and will use the guidance you just provided\nfor future videos. Seems like a great device, very high quality. I noticed\nthat it requires a little wait time for a move to register. In other words,\nif I move a piece and hit the clock too quickly, the move doesn't register.\nSo I've been making my move, then waiting 2-3 seconds before hitting the\nclock. This is not ideal if you're trying to play quickly, but I saw\nthere's a setting that might change this, so maybe I need to explore more.\n\nThanks!\nMarc\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/DZrM6qNyzwk/\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/DZ6WcwmDtoI/\n\nOn Thu, Jun 25, 2026 at 3:10 AM Stella Zhuang\nwrote:\n\n> Hi everyone,\n>\n> I hope this email finds you well!\n>\n> 1. Have you received the Chessnut Companion yet? If you have, we’d love to\n> hear your first impressions! If not, please let us know and we’ll track it\n> for you.\n>\n> 2. Please find attached the Companion brief for your reference. It covers\n> the key selling points, suggested content angles, and video requirements —\n> feel free to use it as a guide for your upcoming content.\n>\n> 3. A quick note on the AI Coach feature: it’s not fully ready just yet and\n> is currently expected to be completed around next week. You can hold off on\n> filming that part until it’s ready.\n>\n> 4. Also, a new version of the app will be launching soon with several\n> updated sections. Stay tuned — we’ll share more details when it’s live.\n>\n> Let us know if you have any questions!\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n\nHi, Stella, Yes, I&#39;ve received the companion. It&#39;s very cool. I&#39;ve posted a couple of videos already (links below) and will use the guidance you just provided for future videos. Seems like a great device, very high quality. I noticed that it requires a little wait time for a move to register. In other words, if I move a piece and hit the clock too quickly, the move doesn&#39;t register. So I&#39;ve been making my move, then waiting 2-3 seconds before hitting the clock. This is not ideal if you&#39;re trying to play quickly, but I saw there&#39;s a setting that might change this, so maybe I need to explore more.  Thanks! Marc https://www.instagram.com/p/DZrM6qNyzwk/ https://www.instagram.com/p/DZ6WcwmDtoI/ On Thu, Jun 25, 2026 at 3:10 AM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi everyone, I hope this email finds you well! 1. Have you received the Chessnut Companion yet? If you have, we’d love to hear your first impressions! If not, please let us know and we’ll track it for you. 2. Please find attached the Companion brief for your reference. It covers the key selling points, suggested content angles, and video requirements — feel free to use it as a guide for your upcoming content. 3. A quick note on the AI Coach feature: it’s not fully ready just yet and is currently expected to be completed around next week. You can hold off on filming that part until it’s ready. 4. Also, a new version of the app will be launching soon with several updated sections. Stay tuned — we’ll share more details when it’s live. Let us know if you have any questions! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut",
      "bodyChinese": "Hi, Stella,\n\nYes, I've received the companion. It's very cool. I've posted a couple of\nvideos already (links below) and will use the guidance you just provided\nfor future videos. Seems like a great device, very high quality. I noticed\nthat it requires a little wait time for a move to register. In other words,\nif I move a piece and hit the clock too quickly, the move doesn't register.\nSo I've been making my move, then waiting 2-3 seconds before hitting the\nclock. This is not ideal if you're trying to play quickly, but I saw\nthere's a setting that might change this, so maybe I need to explore more.\n\nThanks!\nMarc\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/DZrM6qNyzwk/\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/DZ6WcwmDtoI/\n\nOn Thu, Jun 25, 2026 at 3:10 AM Stella Zhuang\nwrote:\n\n> Hi everyone,\n>\n> I hope this email finds you well!\n>\n> 1. Have you received the Chessnut Companion yet? If you have, we’d love to\n> hear your first impressions! If not, please let us know and we’ll track it\n> for you.\n>\n> 2. Please find attached the Companion brief for your reference. It covers\n> the key selling points, suggested content angles, and video requirements —\n> feel free to use it as a guide for your upcoming content.\n>\n> 3. A quick note on the AI Coach feature: it’s not fully ready just yet and\n> is currently expected to be completed around next week. You can hold off on\n> filming that part until it’s ready.\n>\n> 4. Also, a new version of the app will be launching soon with several\n> updated sections. Stay tuned — we’ll share more details when it’s live.\n>\n> Let us know if you have any questions!\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n\nHi, Stella, Yes, I&#39;ve received the companion. It&#39;s very cool. I&#39;ve posted a couple of videos already (links below) and will use the guidance you just provided for future videos. Seems like a great device, very high quality. I noticed that it requires a little wait time for a move to register. In other words, if I move a piece and hit the clock too quickly, the move doesn&#39;t register. So I&#39;ve been making my move, then waiting 2-3 seconds before hitting the clock. This is not ideal if you&#39;re trying to play quickly, but I saw there&#39;s a setting that might change this, so maybe I need to explore more.  Thanks! Marc https://www.instagram.com/p/DZrM6qNyzwk/ https://www.instagram.com/p/DZ6WcwmDtoI/ On Thu, Jun 25, 2026 at 3:10 AM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi everyone, I hope this email finds you well! 1. Have you received the Chessnut Companion yet? If you have, we’d love to hear your first impressions! If not, please let us know and we’ll track it for you. 2. Please find attached the Companion brief for your reference. It covers the key selling points, suggested content angles, and video requirements — feel free to use it as a guide for your upcoming content. 3. A quick note on the AI Coach feature: it’s not fully ready just yet and is currently expected to be completed around next week. You can hold off on filming that part until it’s ready. 4. Also, a new version of the app will be launching soon with several updated sections. Stay tuned — we’ll share more details when it’s live. Let us know if you have any questions! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut",
