      "body": "Hi Stella,\n\nThank you so much! Everything looks great on our end! We updated our payout details as well. Thanks again!\n\nWarmest regards,\nTammy\n\n> On Jun 25, 2026, at 2:57 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> Thanks for confirming! I’ve already adjusted your commission to 10% — please check on your end.\n>\n>\n> Also, please make sure to fill in your payout details. Chessnut processes payments at the beginning of each month for the previous month’s commissions.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 15:39\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Thank you so much! We have registered under the email address: partner@blackmediapresents.com\n>\n> Thanks again and we are looking forward to what’s to come!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n>\n> On Jun 24, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> Thank you for the clarification — I really appreciate it. And yes, 10% works perfectly for us.\n> To get started, please go ahead and register through the link I shared earlier. Once you’ve registered, just send me the email address you used, and I’ll adjust your commission to 10% on our end.\n> As for the sponsored live stream series — we’re not looking to explore that at this stage, but we’re excited to move forward with the studio integration and affiliate collaboration.\n> Let me know once you’ve registered!\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：Black Media Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年6月24日(周三) 06:44\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Thank you so much for taking the time to share your concerns. Looking back at how I laid out our options, I can see how it may have read as tying the studio access to a paid package. That was not my intention at all, and I am sorry for the confusion. I want to clear things up because we are absolutely still on the same page as where we started.\n>\n> The studio integration and product placement is very much our intention and always has been. The chess board is in the studio, we've been demonstrating it to Howie and our guests, and everyone who sees it in action is blown away. That organic exposure, as well as any press, TV coverage, interviews, or a guest trying it out, is still what we're doing. If any of that finds its way into press, TV, or social media naturally, that is exactly what we want to provide in exchange for you sending the boards.\n>\n> Regarding the flat fee and higher commission mention, that was specific to a separate format entirely: targeted, sales-focused social media videos designed to convert using our affiliate link. Those dedicated posts require a different level of creative investment and are built to drive direct sales, which is why the compensation structure looks different for that format. That said, we actually prefer the commission route over a flat fee, and we are fully on board with the 10%. None of this affects the studio integration, which remains exactly as we originally discussed.\n>\n> The one additional idea we wanted to put on the table, and only if you have budget for it in the future, is a sponsored live stream series. This would look like longer-form live chess streams on TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, etc., two to three times a month, with the possibility of bringing in celebrity guests to play. That would be a separate paid sponsorship conversation, and entirely optional. If it is not in the budget, no worries at all. It does not affect anything we already have in place; we just feel it could be incredible exposure and could really increase sales.\n>\n> We are so excited about this partnership and want it to feel as good on your end as it does on ours. Please let us know if you have any questions and also when we can get started with the SUNNYLOVE code and 10% commission!\n>\n> Thank you so much.\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Jun 23, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> I just want to make sure I understand correctly. In our earlier conversations, the idea was that Chessnut boards would be placed naturally in the studio — as part of the background in interviews, or as something that might come up organically if Howie or other guests noticed them. That’s the kind of exposure we were originally excited about.\n> Now it seems like we’re being offered paid social media content instead. That’s a very different direction from what we discussed earlier.\n> To be direct: paid content isn’t something we can consider. And on the commission side, our maximum is 10% — that’s the highest we offer.\n> We’d still love to explore the studio integration — having Chessnut boards appear naturally in the background of interviews or studio content, with the possibility of organic moments with Howie or other talent. That kind of authentic exposure is what we’d really like to focus on.\n> If that’s still possible, we’re happy to continue the conversation. If not, we completely understand — and we can leave it here.\n> Let us know your thoughts.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年6月17日(周三) 13:20\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Thank you so much for your message. We are so excited about Chessnut and truly believe in what you have built.\n>\n> Before we finalize everything, we wanted to share how we typically structure our brand partnerships so we can find the right fit for both sides. We have two options depending on what works best for Chessnut:\n>\n> Option A: Performance-Based Partnership\n>\n> A 20% affiliate commission with no flat fee. This is our partnership track, where we are both fully invested in driving sales. You pay nothing upfront, and we are motivated to push the product through our social media channels because our earnings are tied directly to performance.\n>\n> Option B: Guaranteed Content Package\n>\n> A 5% affiliate commission plus a flat fee of $4,000 per dedicated short-form video. This option gives you guaranteed, high-quality content delivered to our combined audience of 1.9 million followers across Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, and YouTube, regardless of conversion. It also includes the organic celebrity and press exposure we have access to through Howie Mandel's studio, which is something truly unique to us.\n>\n> One additional benefit worth mentioning: through our access at Howie Mandel's studio, celebrity content opportunities come up organically. When they do, we will reach out with the details and give you the option to add it on as a dedicated piece of content. Two of the primary celebrity formats would be 1) when a celebrity engages with and responds to seeing Chessnut in action in real time, and 2) product gifting videos, where we demonstrate the board and gift a Chessnut to the celebrity on camera (this requires having a small stock on hand). The gifting format in particular tends to create warm, heartfelt moments that highlight the product naturally, and often results in the celebrity posting about it on their own channels at a later date, extending the reach of the content well beyond our own audience. These opportunities typically start at $10,000, and as a partner we would offer those to you at a reduced rate.\n>\n> Both options come with our full creative investment and the SUNNYLOVE affiliate code active and promoted across our content and community.\n>\n> We would love to hear which structure feels like the best fit on your end, and we are happy to talk through either option in more detail.\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Jun 10, 2026, at 12:53 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> Thanks for reaching out, Tammy. Really glad to hear how excited you are about the Chessnut Move!\n>\n> Yes, we do have an affiliate program, and you're very welcome to join. You can sign up through Uppromote, which is the platform we use to manage and track affiliate sales.\n>\n> Here's the registration link:\n> https://af.uppromote.com/Chessnutech/register\n>\n> Once you're in, you can create your own discount code. You're welcome to name it SUNNYLOVE. The code will offer a 12% discount (our official site discount is 10%), and you'll earn a 5% commission on sales generated through your code. Commissions are paid out at the beginning of each month.\n>\n> Let me know if you run into any issues during sign-up. Happy to help!\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年6月10日(周三) 05:03\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> I just wanted to check in on my previous email. We are so excited about the Chessnut Move and would love to follow up on our question about an affiliate code. We would love to promote Chessnut to our audience and community.\n>\n> Please let me know if you need anything from our end. We appreciate you!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Jun 3, 2026, at 4:27 PM, BlackMedia Partnerships wrote:\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> We set up the plastic chess board last night and were absolutely blown away. It is so unique and genuinely feels like we are living in the future we dreamed of as children. Chessnut is a game changer, and the world needs to know about it.\n>\n> We want to actively promote Chessnut to our audience and community and make it a brand they know, trust, and buy. Our audience follows Sunny's recommendations closely, and when we get behind something, they are eager to check it out.\n>\n> On that note, we wanted to ask about your affiliate structure. We use the code SUNNYLOVE across all of our brand partnerships, and our community has really come to know and trust it. If you are able to set us up with SUNNYLOVE as a coupon and affiliate code, we would love to understand the discount and commission breakdown on your end so we can start building out a strategy around it.\n>\n> Thank you again for sending these boards. We are so excited about what we can build together, and we cannot wait to show it to Howie!\n>\n> Warm regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Jun 2, 2026, at 6:17 PM, Black Media Partnerships wrote:\n>\n> Hi Stella!\n>\n> Thank you so much for updating us on the shipment. We have received it safely and can’t wait to open them up and get everything set up. We truly appreciate it and will be in touch soon!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Jun 2, 2026, at 12:59 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> Both the wooden and plastic Move boards have been sent. Tracking number: 1Z4E2W090327952423. Carrier: UPS.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年5月7日(周四) 16:25\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Hope you have been doing well! We are still very much looking forward to receiving the chess boards as soon as they are available. I wanted to take a moment to share some exciting updates from the studio!\n>\n> Since we last spoke, we have had some incredible guests come through, including Joey Fatone from *NSYNC and Academy Award winner Billy Bob Thornton, who was even photographed with Sunny's Signature Ukulele. We would have absolutely loved to have had your chess board on display!\n>\n> Please do keep us posted on availability!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> Billy Bob Thornton of Landman, Bad Santa, Sling Blade\n>\n>\n> Joey Fatone of *NSYNC\n>\n>\n> On Apr 23, 2026, at 10:50 AM, Black Media Partnerships wrote:\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Thank you so much! We are looking forward to it, hope you have a wonderful day!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Apr 22, 2026, at 11:05 PM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> Got it, thank you!\n> I'll share the tracking number with you as soon as I have it.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年4月23日(周四) 05:29\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Thank you so much, that all sounds wonderful. We completely understand the inventory shortages and are very much looking forward to receiving the units (one wood, one plastic) whenever they are ready!\n>\n> Shipping info:\n>\n> Sunny Promyotin\n> 5317 Shirley Ave\n> Tarzana, CA 91356\n> Phone: (415) 810-3060\n>\n> Thank you very much and looking forward to what’s to come!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Apr 22, 2026, at 2:39 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> Thanks so much for your detailed response – really appreciate it.\n>\n> Could you please share the recipient's full name, shipping address, and postal code? Ideally a non-business address if possible, just to ensure smooth delivery.\n>\n> One thing I need to let you know upfront – our US warehouse is currently facing a serious inventory shortage, so the two Chessnut Move units (one wood, one plastic) are not in stock at the moment. We expect them to be available around late May, and we will ship them out as soon as they're ready.\n>\n> I hope this timeline still works for you. Please let me know if you have any questions.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：Black Media Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年4月18日(周六) 15:24\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Thank you so much for your questions! To give you a bit of context on our setup, as the Official House Band and Gaming Team of Howie Mandel, the partnership would be between Chessnut and Sunny and The Black Pack directly. Because we operate out of Howie's studio, Howie does interact with everything we bring in, and if he loves it, that kind of organic exposure is very possible, though not guaranteed. We are looking to get the chess boards into the studio as soon as possible with testing occurring over the next couple weeks.\n>\n> Following the testing period, if Sunny loves it, we can build out a realistic and well-rounded partnership plan together. Some of which could include social media content such as reels and stories across our platforms (over 1.8M followers), studio product placement, targeted celebrity gifting, etc. But we would have a much clearer idea after testing it out in the environment.\n>\n> We love the recommendation of two Chessnut Move units, one with wooden pieces and one with plastic. That variety gives us great options visually and the auto-moving will be extremely engaging and striking in-person and on camera.\n>\n> Thank you so much!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n>\n> On Apr 17, 2026, at 1:54 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> Thanks for the message — we're excited too.\n>\n> Just a few quick questions:\n>\n> When are you thinking of testing the boards? (rough timeline)\n>\n> If Howie likes it, what kind of exposure are you expecting? (IG post, podcast, video, etc.)\n>\n> After testing, what kind of collab do you have in mind? (product placement, content, etc.)\n>\n> We recommend sending two Chessnut Move units — one with wooden pieces, one with plastic pieces. Same model, different look. The auto-moving feature is great for camera.\n>\n> Let us know your thoughts.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年4月17日(周五) 15:45\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> I wanted to check in and see if you had any questions or thoughts on everything we shared. We are very excited about the possibilities here and happy to chat through anything!\n>\n> Looking forward to hearing from you!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Apr 10, 2026, at 2:41 AM, BlackMedia Partnerships wrote:\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Thank you so much for your thoughtful response. We are very excited about what's possible here!\n>\n> To best understand what's realistic and structure a partnership that truly suits Chessnut, we'd love to start by testing two units, one at Howie's studio and one at our sister studio, both of which have a steady flow of celebrity guests and filming sets. One of our top priorities would be getting Chessnut in front of Howie so he can personally experience it. This would also let us see how the boards look on our sets, how they integrate organically into the studio environment, and test the functionality with our full team.\n>\n> If this sounds good to you, we'd love your recommendation on the two models you feel would be most visually striking on camera and most impressive in person, the ones that would really create that wow-factor for celebrities and social media alike. You know your product better than anyone, and we want to make sure we would be showcasing Chessnut in the best possible light.\n>\n> From there, we can build out a realistic and well-rounded partnership plan together.\n>\n> Looking forward to hearing your thoughts!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n>\n> Tammy Byerly\n> Strategic Partnerships\n> Black Media Co., LLC\n> https://linktr.ee/BlackMediaContact\n>\n>\n> On Apr 9, 2026, at 5:12 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> Thanks again for the detailed introduction — really impressive network you've built.\n>\n> What caught our attention most is your access to Howie Mandel's ecosystem:\n>\n> The podcast (Howie Mandel Does Stuff)\n>\n> The LA studio with celebrity guests\n>\n> GGL and the celebrity gaming league\n>\n> If a partnership can tap into those — for example, product placement in the studio, a mention on the podcast, or Howie/Sunny naturally using Chessnut in content — that's where we see the real value.\n>\n> Could you help us understand what's realistic here, and what kind of partnership you had in mind?\n>\n> Looking forward to your thoughts.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年4月8日(周三) 04:16\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Dear Stella,\n>\n> Vincent Lo gave me your email address so I could contact you about partnership opportunties with Chessnut. We’ve been following Chessnut's journey and think what you're building is brilliant and beautifully crafted. We really admire what you’re doing to revolutionize chess. I'm Tammy, and I work on Strategic Partnerships for Sunny and The Black Pack, the Official House Band & Gaming Team of Howie Mandel (of the hit shows America’s Got Talents and Deal or No Deal). We are also part of the Global Gaming League alongside T-Pain. We'd love to connect and explore what opportunities there might be to partner with Chessnut.\n>\n> We work out of Howie's studio in Los Angeles, which is an incredible playground of music, cutting-edge technology, art, and entertainment, with frequent high-profile celebrity guests. Within the studio, we live stream, film TV shows, music videos, and podcasts, including podcasts hosted by Howie Mandel, Billy Corgan of The Smashing Pumpkins, Jack Osbourne, Jillian Michaels, Billy Bush, and Holly Madison. We are part of Howie's podcast Howie Mandel Does Stuff, with guests like Sofia Vergara of Modern Family, Heidi Klum, Terry Crews, Simon Cowell, Tim Allen, Kris Jenner, Oliver Tree and many more.\n>\n> Some links to help you get to know us better:\n>\n> Global Gaming League (we are team “Howie Do It”): https://youtu.be/diBz3ZrWDpM\n> Michael Bublé with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://youtu.be/KdZpc87sQ7o\n> Richie Sambora of Bon Jovi with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://youtu.be/arei8ZOEdOw\n> Logic with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://youtu.be/XLai0lZHN5I\n> Gene Simmons of KISS with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://www.instagram.com/p/DE0PUYlyrqE/\n> Rob Lowe with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DMIRzDlOzTb/\n> Arsenio Hall with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DAGrx6tvFBk/\n> Jason Alexander of Seinfeld bass gift: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DBHF7VgvqE4/\n> Skechers Holiday TV Ad starred in and wrote and recorded music: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DRxjIs7Eth8/\n>\n> We have over 1.8 million followers across platforms and influential followers like Howie Mandel, Michael Bublé, David Arquette, Arsenio Hall, Danny Trejo, Tom Green, Paula Abdul, Adrian Grenier, Zedd, The Sound of Music, Sal Vulcano, Kenny Loggins, Kurt Sutter, Robert and Dean DeLeo of Stone Temple Pilots, Dick Van Dyke, Gary Busey, Ray J, Kevin Nealon of Saturday Night Live and many others.\n>\n> Instagram (399K Followers): https://www.instagram.com/blackmediapresents\n> Facebook (811K Followers): https://www.facebook.com/sunnyandtheblackpack\n> TikTok (591K Followers): https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmediapresents\n> YouTube (64K Subscribers): https://www.youtube.com/blackmediapresents\n>\n> Here are links to collaborations, along with our social channels:\n> https://linktr.ee/BlackMediaContact\n>\n> We'd love to explore ways we can bring Chessnut to even more people through content, studio integration, social media, and celebrity moments. Please let us know if you have any ideas or if you’d like to schedule a Google Meet so we can discuss further.\n>\n> Thank you so much!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n>\n> Tammy Byerly\n> Strategic Partnerships\n> Black Media Co., LLC\n> https://linktr.ee/BlackMediaContact\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n\n--Apple-Mail=_69245FC9-1272-4B4A-9CDB-349CF0C95CB3\nContent-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable\nContent-Type: text/html;\ncharset=utf-8\n\nHi Stella, Thank you so much! Everything looks great on our end! We updated our payout details as well. Thanks again! Warmest regards, Tammy On Jun 25, 2026, at 2:57 AM, Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: Hi Tammy, Thanks for confirming! I’ve already adjusted your commission to 10% — please check on your end. &lt;temp4cj.png&gt; Also, please make sure to fill in your payout details. Chessnut processes payments at the beginning of each month for the previous month’s commissions. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships &lt;partner@blackmediapresents.com&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 15:39 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry Hi Stella, Thank you so much! We have registered under the email address: partner@blackmediapresents.com &nbsp; Thanks again and we are looking forward to what’s to come! Warmest regards, Tammy On Jun 24, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: Hi Tammy, Thank you for the clarification — I really appreciate it. And yes, 10% works perfectly for us. To get started, please go ahead and register through the link I shared earlier. Once you’ve registered, just send me the email address you used, and I’ll adjust your commission to 10% on our end. As for the sponsored live stream series — we’re not looking to explore that at this stage, but we’re excited to move forward with the studio integration and affiliate collaboration. Let me know once you’ve registered! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Black Media Partnerships &lt;partner@blackmediapresents.com&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月24日(周三) 06:44 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry Hi Stella, Thank you so much for taking the time to share your concerns. Looking back at how I laid out our options, I can see how it may have read as tying the studio access to a paid package. That was not my intention at all, and I am sorry for the confusion. I want to clear things up because we are absolutely still on the same page as where we started. The studio integration and product placement is very much our intention and always has been. The chess board is in the studio, we've been demonstrating it to Howie and our guests, and everyone who sees it in action is blown away. That organic exposure, as well as any press, TV coverage, interviews, or a guest trying it out, is still what we're doing. If any of that finds its way into press, TV, or social media naturally, that is exactly what we want to provide in exchange for you sending the boards. Regarding the flat fee and higher commission mention, that was specific to a separate format entirely: targeted, sales-focused social media videos designed to convert using our affiliate link. Those dedicated posts require a different level of creative investment and are built to drive direct sales, which is why the compensation structure looks different for that format. That said, we actually prefer the commission route over a flat fee, and we are fully on board with the 10%. None of this affects the studio integration, which remains exactly as we originally discussed. The one additional idea we wanted to put on the table, and only if you have budget for it in the future, is a sponsored live stream series. This would look like longer-form live chess streams on TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, etc., two to three times a month, with the possibility of bringing in celebrity guests to play. That would be a separate paid sponsorship conversation, and entirely optional. If it is not in the budget, no worries at all. It does not affect anything we already have in place; we just feel it could be incredible exposure and could really increase sales. We are so excited about this partnership and want it to feel as good on your end as it does on ours. Please let us know if you have any questions and also when we can get started with the SUNNYLOVE code and 10% commission! Thank you so much. Warmest regards, Tammy On Jun 23, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: ﻿ Hi Tammy, I just want to make sure I understand correctly. In our earlier conversations, the idea was that Chessnut boards would be placed naturally in the studio — as part of the background in interviews, or as something that might come up organically if Howie or other guests noticed them. That’s the kind of exposure we were originally excited about. Now it seems like we’re being offered paid social media content instead. That’s a very different direction from what we discussed earlier. To be direct: paid content isn’t something we can consider. And on the commission side, our maximum is 10% — that’s the highest we offer. We’d still love to explore the studio integration — having Chessnut boards appear naturally in the background of interviews or studio content, with the possibility of organic moments with Howie or other talent. That kind of authentic exposure is what we’d really like to focus on. If that’s still possible, we’re happy to continue the conversation. If not, we completely understand — and we can leave it here. Let us know your thoughts. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：BlackMed