o move forward with the studio integration and affiliate collaboration. Let me know once you’ve registered! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Black Media Partnerships &lt;partner@blackmediapresents.com&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月24日(周三) 06:44 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry Hi Stella, Thank you so much for taking the time to share your concerns. Looking back at how I laid out our options, I can see how it may have read as tying the studio access to a paid package. That was not my intention at all, and I am sorry for the confusion. I want to clear things up because we are absolutely still on the same page as where we started. The studio integration and product placement is very much our intention and always has been. The chess board is in the studio, we've been demonstrating it to Howie and our guests, and everyone who sees it in action is blown away. That organic exposure, as well as any press, TV coverage, interviews, or a guest trying it out, is still what we're doing. If any of that finds its way into press, TV, or social media naturally, that is exactly what we want to provide in exchange for you sending the boards. Regarding the flat fee and higher commission mention, that was specific to a separate format entirely: targeted, sales-focused social media videos designed to convert using our affiliate link. Those dedicated posts require a different level of creative investment and are built to drive direct sales, which is why the compensation structure looks different for that format. That said, we actually prefer the commission route over a flat fee, and we are fully on board with the 10%. None of this affects the studio integration, which remains exactly as we originally discussed. The one additional idea we wanted to put on the table, and only if you have budget for it in the future, is a sponsored live stream series. This would look like longer-form live chess streams on TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, etc., two to three times a month, with the possibility of bringing in celebrity guests to play. That would be a separate paid sponsorship conversation, and entirely optional. If it is not in the budget, no worries at all. It does not affect anything we already have in place; we just feel it could be incredible exposure and could really increase sales. We are so excited about this partnership and want it to feel as good on your end as it does on ours. Please let us know if you have any questions and also when we can get started with the SUNNYLOVE code and 10% commission! Thank you so much. Warmest regards, Tammy On Jun 23, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: ﻿ Hi Tammy, I just want to make sure I understand correctly. In our earlier conversations, the idea was that Chessnut boards would be placed naturally in the studio — as part of the background in interviews, or as something that might come up organically if Howie or other guests noticed them. That’s the kind of exposure we were originally excited about. Now it seems like we’re being offered paid social media content instead. That’s a very different direction from what we discussed earlier. To be direct: paid content isn’t something we can consider. And on the commission side, our maximum is 10% — that’s the highest we offer. We’d still love to explore the studio integration — having Chessnut boards appear naturally in the background of interviews or studio content, with the possibility of organic moments with Howie or other talent. That kind of authentic exposure is what we’d really like to focus on. If that’s still possible, we’re happy to continue the conversation. If not, we completely understand — and we can leave it here. Let us know your thoughts. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：B