gaging and striking in-person and on camera. Thank you so much! Warmest regards, Tammy On Apr 17, 2026, at 1:54 AM, Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: ﻿ Hi Tammy, Thanks for the message — we're excited too. Just a few quick questions: When are you thinking of testing the boards? (rough timeline) If Howie likes it, what kind of exposure are you expecting? (IG post, podcast, video, etc.) After testing, what kind of collab do you have in mind? (product placement, content, etc.) We recommend sending two Chessnut Move units — one with wooden pieces, one with plastic pieces. Same model, different look. The auto-moving feature is great for camera. Let us know your thoughts. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships &lt;partner@blackmediapresents.com&gt; 发送时间：2026年4月17日(周五) 15:45 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry Hi Stella, I wanted to check in and see if you had any questions or thoughts on everything we shared. We are very excited about the possibilities here and happy to chat through anything! Looking forward to hearing from you! Warmest regards, Tammy On Apr 10, 2026, at 2:41 AM, BlackMedia Partnerships &lt;partner@blackmediapresents.com&gt; wrote: Hi Stella, Thank you so much for your thoughtful response. We are very excited about what's possible here! To best understand what's realistic and structure a partnership that truly suits Chessnut, we'd love to start by testing two units, one at Howie's studio and one at our sister studio, both of which have a steady flow of celebrity guests and filming sets. One of our top priorities would be getting Chessnut in front of Howie so he can personally experience it. This would also let us see how the boards look on our sets, how they integrate organically into the studio environment, and test the functionality with our full team. If this sounds good to you, we'd love your recommendation on the two models you feel would be most visually striking on camera and most impressive in person, the ones that would really create that wow-factor for celebrities and social media alike. You know your product better than anyone, and we want to make sure we would be showcasing Chessnut in the best possible light. From there, we can build out a realistic and well-rounded partnership plan together. Looking forward to hearing your thoughts! Warmest regards, Tammy Byerly Strategic Partnerships Black Media Co., LLC https://linktr.ee/BlackMediaContact On Apr 9, 2026, at 5:12 AM, Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: Hi Tammy, Thanks again for the detailed introduction — really impressive network you've built. What caught our attention most is your access to Howie Mandel's ecosystem: The podcast (Howie Mandel Does Stuff) The LA studio with celebrity guests GGL and the celebrity gaming league If a partnership can tap into those — for example, product placement in the studio, a mention on the podcast, or Howie/Sunny naturally using Chessnut in content — that's where we see the real value. Could you help us understand what's realistic here, and what kind of partnership you had in mind? Looking forward to your thoughts. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships &lt;partner@blackmediapresents.com&gt; 发送时间：2026年4月8日(周三) 04:16 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主　题：Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry Dear Stella, Vincent Lo gave me your email address so I could contact you about partnership opportunties with Chessnut. We’ve been following Chessnut's journey and think what you're building is brilliant and beautifully crafted. We really admire what you’re doing to revolutionize chess. I'm Tammy, and I work on Strategic Partnerships for&nbsp; Sunny and 