 3 Chessnut boards be used across the 10 tournaments? Will they be awarded at the final Grand Prix standings, or distributed across individual events? - If there are other sponsors, will the Chessnut boards be presented as standalone prizes, or grouped together with other sponsor items? Also, could you confirm the timeline for Marianczello’s YouTube videos and mentions? Looking forward to your reply! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl &lt;krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 18:36 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主　题：Odp: 回复：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series Hi Stella, I am the lead organizer and creator of this event, as well as the administrator of the MARIANCZELLO Club on Chess.com . Marianczello and I are close friends; he was actually my very first chess coach. This entire cycle is being organized to celebrate his 10th anniversary as a content creator. To answer your questions directly: Role &amp; Structure: I operate independently but with Marianczello's full backing. This is a non-profit project driven entirely by my passion to popularize chess. There are no entry fees, and I am not making any profit from it. Tournament Format: It is a hybrid Grand Prix system consisting of 10 monthly editions . In each standalone edition, the top 3 players win prizes, and additional sponsor items are raffled among all participants. Concurrently, the top 30 players from each edition earn points toward a general Grand Prix standing. The biggest guaranteed prizes are reserved for the overall Top 6, alongside a separate raffle pool for active club members. Timeline: We kick off this Sunday, June 28 . Each subsequent edition will take place on the last Sunday of every month, concluding with the grand finale in March 2027 . Player Turnout &amp; Registration: The event is officially hosted on the Chess.com Events platform. Because of how the platform works, official player registration opens exactly one hour before the tournament starts. However, based on our club's active community size, we are expecting a very strong turnout. Exposure &amp; Marketing: We have fantastic channels lined up! Chess.com Polska has already published information about our tournament and will promote it again right before the launch. Additionally, Marianczello will be live-streaming parts of the tournament cycle (schedule permitting). We are also planning to include dedicated sponsor mentions and product placements directly inside Marianczello’s upcoming YouTube videos. Regarding your mention of co-creating content, could you please provide more details on what exactly you have in mind? Once I have more specifics, I will consult directly with Marianczello to see what formats we can best integrate into his channel. Please let me know if this structure aligns with Chessnut's goals, and we can discuss how to move forward! Best regards, Krzysztof Lead Organizer | MARIANCZELLO Club\n\nDnia 25 czerwca 2026 12:07\nStella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; napisał(a):\n\nHi Krzysztof, Thanks for the detailed proposal — it sounds like a well-structured event with strong community backing. Before we move forward, I have a few questions: - Are you part of Marianczello’s team, or an independent organizer working with him? - Could you clarify the structure of the 10-tournament cycle? Is it 10 separate events with their own winners, or a points-based series leading to one overall champion? - Roughly how many players have registered so far? - You mentioned that 3 boards would help ‘create massive buzz across the 10-tournament cycle’ — could you clarify what the exposure channels look like? Are there social media promotions, media coverage, or other content formats? We’d also be open to co-creating content together. This will help us get a clearer picture and move forward more confidently. Best, Stella Business Developmen