 Inquiry Dear Stella, Vincent Lo gave me your email address so I could contact you about partnership opportunties with Chessnut. We’ve been following Chessnut's journey and think what you're building is brilliant and beautifully crafted. We really admire what you’re doing to revolutionize chess. I'm Tammy, and I work on Strategic Partnerships for&nbsp; Sunny and The Black Pack, the Official House Band &amp; Gaming Team of Howie Mandel &nbsp;(of the hit shows America’s Got Talents and Deal or No Deal). We are also part of the Global Gaming League alongside T-Pain. We'd love to connect and explore what opportunities there might be to partner with Chessnut. We work out of Howie's studio in Los Angeles, which is an incredible playground of music, cutting-edge technology, art, and entertainment, with frequent high-profile celebrity guests. Within the studio, we live stream, film TV shows, music videos, and podcasts, including podcasts hosted by Howie Mandel, Billy Corgan of The Smashing Pumpkins, Jack Osbourne, Jillian Michaels, Billy Bush, and Holly Madison. We are part of Howie's podcast Howie Mandel Does Stuff, with guests like Sofia Vergara of Modern Family, Heidi Klum, Terry Crews, Simon Cowell, Tim Allen, Kris Jenner, Oliver Tree and many more. Some links to help you get to know us better: Global Gaming League &nbsp;(we are team “Howie Do It”):&nbsp; https://youtu.be/diBz3ZrWDpM Michael Bublé &nbsp;with Sunny and The Black Pack:&nbsp; https://youtu.be/KdZpc87sQ7o Richie Sambora of Bon Jovi&nbsp; with Sunny and The Black Pack:&nbsp; https://youtu.be/arei8ZOEdOw Logic &nbsp;with Sunny and The Black Pack:&nbsp; https://youtu.be/XLai0lZHN5I Gene Simmons of KISS &nbsp;with Sunny and The Black Pack:&nbsp; https://www.instagram.com/p/DE0PUYlyrqE/ Rob Lowe &nbsp;with Sunny and The Black Pack:&nbsp; https://www.instagram.com/reel/DMIRzDlOzTb/ Arsenio Hall&nbsp; with Sunny and The Black Pack:&nbsp; https://www.instagram.com/reel/DAGrx6tvFBk/ Jason Alexander of Seinfeld &nbsp;bass gift:&nbsp; https://www.instagram.com/reel/DBHF7VgvqE4/ Skechers Holiday TV Ad&nbsp; starred in and wrote and recorded music:&nbsp; https://www.instagram.com/reel/DRxjIs7Eth8/ We have over 1.8 million followers across platforms and influential followers like Howie Mandel, Michael Bublé, David Arquette, Arsenio Hall, Danny Trejo, Tom Green, Paula Abdul, Adrian Grenier, Zedd, The Sound of Music, Sal Vulcano, Kenny Loggins, Kurt Sutter, Robert and Dean DeLeo of Stone Temple Pilots, Dick Van Dyke, Gary Busey, Ray J, Kevin Nealon of Saturday Night Live and many others. Instagram (399K Followers):&nbsp; https://www.instagram.com/blackmediapresents Facebook (811K Followers):&nbsp; https://www.facebook.com/sunnyandtheblackpack TikTok (591K Followers):&nbsp; https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmediapresents YouTube (64K Subscribers):&nbsp; https://www.youtube.com/blackmediapresents Here are links to collaborations, along with our social channels: https://linktr.ee/BlackMediaContact We'd love to explore ways we can bring Chessnut to even more people through content, studio integration, social media, and celebrity moments. Please let us know if you have any ideas or if you’d like to schedule a Google Meet so we can discuss further.&nbsp; Thank you so much! Warmest regards, Tammy Byerly Strategic Partnerships Black Media Co., LLC https://linktr.ee/BlackMediaContact\n--Apple-Mail=_B64702BE-9C06-456A-BDE2-40A0B3EC6B32--",
      "bodyChinese": "Hi Stella,\n\nThank you so much! We have registered under the email address: partner@blackmediapresents.com\n\nThanks again and we are looking forward to what’s to come!\n\nWarmest regards,\nTammy\n\n> On Jun 24, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> Thank you for the clarification — I really appreciate it. And yes, 10% works perfectly for us.\n> To get started, please go ahead and register through the link I shared earlier. Once you’ve registered, just send me the email address you used, and I’ll adjust your commission to 10% on our end.\n> As for the sponsored live stream series — we’re not looking to explore that at this stage, but we’re excited to move forward with the studio integration and affiliate collaboration.\n> Let me know once you’ve registered!\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：Black Media Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年6月24日(周三) 06:44\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Thank you so much for taking the time to share your concerns. Looking back at how I laid out our options, I can see how it may have read as tying the studio access to a paid package. That was not my intention at all, and I am sorry for the confusion. I want to clear things up because we are absolutely still on the same page as where we started.\n>\n> The studio integration and product placement is very much our intention and always has been. The chess board is in the studio, we've been demonstrating it to Howie and our guests, and everyone who sees it in action is blown away. That organic exposure, as well as any press, TV coverage, interviews, or a guest trying it out, is still what we're doing. If any of that finds its way into press, TV, or social media naturally, that is exactly what we want to provide in exchange for you sending the boards.\n>\n> Regarding the flat fee and higher commission mention, that was specific to a separate format entirely: targeted, sales-focused social media videos designed to convert using our affiliate link. Those dedicated posts require a different level of creative investment and are built to drive direct sales, which is why the compensation structure looks different for that format. That said, we actually prefer the commission route over a flat fee, and we are fully on board with the 10%. None of this affects the studio integration, which remains exactly as we originally discussed.\n>\n> The one additional idea we wanted to put on the table, and only if you have budget for it in the future, is a sponsored live stream series. This would look like longer-form live chess streams on TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, etc., two to three times a month, with the possibility of bringing in celebrity guests to play. That would be a separate paid sponsorship conversation, and entirely optional. If it is not in the budget, no worries at all. It does not affect anything we already have in place; we just feel it could be incredible exposure and could really increase sales.\n>\n> We are so excited about this partnership and want it to feel as good on your end as it does on ours. Please let us know if you have any questions and also when we can get started with the SUNNYLOVE code and 10% commission!\n>\n> Thank you so much.\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Jun 23, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> I just want to make sure I understand correctly. In our earlier conversations, the idea was that Chessnut boards would be placed naturally in the studio — as part of the background in interviews, or as something that might come up organically if Howie or other guests noticed them. That’s the kind of exposure we were originally excited about.\n> Now it seems like we’re being offered paid social media content instead. That’s a very different direction from what we discussed earlier.\n> To be direct: paid content isn’t something we can consider. And on the commission side, our maximum is 10% — that’s the highest we offer.\n> We’d still love to explore the studio integration — having Chessnut boards appear naturally in the background of interviews or studio content, with the possibility of organic moments with Howie or other talent. That kind of authentic exposure is what we’d really like to focus on.\n> If that’s still possible, we’re happy to continue the conversation. If not, we completely understand — and we can leave it here.\n> Let us know your thoughts.\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年6月17日(周三) 13:20\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> Thank you so much for your message. We are so excited about Chessnut and truly believe in what you have built.\n>\n> Before we finalize everything, we wanted to share how we typically structure our brand partnerships so we can find the right fit for both sides. We have two options depending on what works best for Chessnut:\n>\n> Option A: Performance-Based Partnership\n>\n> A 20% affiliate commission with no flat fee. This is our partnership track, where we are both fully invested in driving sales. You pay nothing upfront, and we are motivated to push the product through our social media channels because our earnings are tied directly to performance.\n>\n> Option B: Guaranteed Content Package\n>\n> A 5% affiliate commission plus a flat fee of $4,000 per dedicated short-form video. This option gives you guaranteed, high-quality content delivered to our combined audience of 1.9 million followers across Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, and YouTube, regardless of conversion. It also includes the organic celebrity and press exposure we have access to through Howie Mandel's studio, which is something truly unique to us.\n>\n> One additional benefit worth mentioning: through our access at Howie Mandel's studio, celebrity content opportunities come up organically. When they do, we will reach out with the details and give you the option to add it on as a dedicated piece of content. Two of the primary celebrity formats would be 1) when a celebrity engages with and responds to seeing Chessnut in action in real time, and 2) product gifting videos, where we demonstrate the board and gift a Chessnut to the celebrity on camera (this requires having a small stock on hand). The gifting format in particular tends to create warm, heartfelt moments that highlight the product naturally, and often results in the celebrity posting about it on their own channels at a later date, extending the reach of the content well beyond our own audience. These opportunities typically start at $10,000, and as a partner we would offer those to you at a reduced rate.\n>\n> Both options come with our full creative investment and the SUNNYLOVE affiliate code active and promoted across our content and community.\n>\n> We would love to hear which structure feels like the best fit on your end, and we are happy to talk through either option in more detail.\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Jun 10, 2026, at 12:53 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote:\n>\n> Hi Tammy,\n>\n> Thanks for reaching out, Tammy. Really glad to hear how excited you are about the Chessnut Move!\n>\n> Yes, we do have an affiliate program, and you're very welcome to join. You can sign up through Uppromote, which is the platform we use to manage and track affiliate sales.\n>\n> Here's the registration link:\n> https://af.uppromote.com/Chessnutech/register\n>\n> Once you're in, you can create your own discount code. You're welcome to name it SUNNYLOVE. The code will offer a 12% discount (our official site discount is 10%), and you'll earn a 5% commission on sales generated through your code. Commissions are paid out at the beginning of each month.\n>\n> Let me know if you run into any issues during sign-up. Happy to help!\n>\n> Best,\n> Stella\n> Business Development Manager | Chessnut\n>\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------\n> 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships\n> 发送时间：2026年6月10日(周三) 05:03\n> 收件人：Stella Zhuang\n> 主　题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> I just wanted to check in on my previous email. We are so excited about the Chessnut Move and would love to follow up on our question about an affiliate code. We would love to promote Chessnut to our audience and community.\n>\n> Please let me know if you need anything from our end. We appreciate you!\n>\n> Warmest regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Jun 3, 2026, at 4:27 PM, BlackMedia Partnerships wrote:\n>\n> Hi Stella,\n>\n> We set up the plastic chess board last night and were absolutely blown away. It is so unique and genuinely feels like we are living in the future we dreamed of as children. Chessnut is a game changer, and the world needs to know about it.\n>\n> We want to actively promote Chessnut to our audience and community and make it a brand they know, trust, and buy. Our audience follows Sunny's recommendations closely, and when we get behind something, they are eager to check it out.\n>\n> On that note, we wanted to ask about your affiliate structure. We use the code SUNNYLOVE across all of our brand partnerships, and our community has really come to know and trust it. If you are able to set us up with SUNNYLOVE as a coupon and affiliate code, we would love to understand the discount and commission breakdown on your end so we can start building out a strategy around it.\n>\n> Thank you again for sending these boards. We are so excited about what we can build together, and we cannot wait to show it to Howie!\n>\n> Warm regards,\n> Tammy\n>\n> On Jun 2, 2026, at 6:17 PM, Black Media Partnerships wrote:\n>\n> Hi Stella!\n>\n> Thank you so much for updating us on the shipment. We have re