ion structure looks different for that format. That said, we actually prefer the commission route over a flat fee, and we are fully on board with the 10%. None of this affects the studio integration, which remains exactly as we originally discussed. The one additional idea we wanted to put on the table, and only if you have budget for it in the future, is a sponsored live stream series. This would look like longer-form live chess streams on TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, etc., two to three times a month, with the possibility of bringing in celebrity guests to play. That would be a separate paid sponsorship conversation, and entirely optional. If it is not in the budget, no worries at all. It does not affect anything we already have in place; we just feel it could be incredible exposure and could really increase sales. We are so excited about this partnership and want it to feel as good on your end as it does on ours. Please let us know if you have any questions and also when we can get started with the SUNNYLOVE code and 10% commission! Thank you so much. Warmest regards, Tammy On Jun 23, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: ﻿ Hi Tammy, I just want to make sure I understand correctly. In our earlier conversations, the idea was that Chessnut boards would be placed naturally in the studio — as part of the background in interviews, or as something that might come up organically if Howie or other guests noticed them. That’s the kind of exposure we were originally excited about. Now it seems like we’re being offered paid social media content instead. That’s a very different direction from what we discussed earlier. To be direct: paid content isn’t something we can consider. And on the commission side, our maximum is 10% — that’s the highest we offer. We’d still love to explore the studio integration — having Chessnut boards appear naturally in the background of interviews or studio content, with the possibility of organic moments with Ho