      "body": "Hello Alan, Thank you very much for your response and for the information you have shared so far. We are interested in continuing our evaluation of Chessnut Move from a commercial, logistics and regulatory perspective in order to properly understand the product's viability in the Mexican market. Before moving forward with any future planning, would it be possible to share the following information? Product Complete technical datasheet for Chessnut Move. Available certifications (FCC, CE, RoHS, etc.). HS Code currently used for export. Commercial Current distributor price for Chessnut Move. Complete Chessnut product catalog. Distributor price list for the full product range. MOQ for future reorder purchases. Current stock availability. Logistics Incoterm normally used for international distributors. Shipping origin city in China. Whether Chessnut normally arranges international transportation for distributors or if distributors typically manage logistics independently. Whether you regularly work with FedEx for international shipments. Whether shipments can be arranged using the customer's FedEx account. Documentation Documentation normally provided for export shipments (Commercial Invoice, Packing List, certificates, declarations, or any other relevant documentation). Warranty &amp; Support Warranty policy for international distributors. Standard procedure for handling warranty claims, replacements, or defective products. We apologize for the number of questions. As part of our evaluation process, we need to fully understand the technical, logistics, regulatory and compliance requirements involved in importing and distributing the product in Mexico. Our goal is to ensure that any future operation is carried out efficiently, professionally and fully within the applicable legal and regulatory framework. Thank you again for your support. We look forward to hearing from you. Best regards, David Mitchel Rios Bernal Popokani México&nbsp;\n\nOn Wed, Jun 24, 2