      "body": "Dear Stella,\n\nthank you very much for your reply — and congratulations on competing in the FIDE Rapid & Blitz Team Championship in Hong Kong! No problem at all about the timing.\n\nI'm glad the idea resonates, and I'd be happy to move both steps forward in parallel.\n\n1) Prizes for players\nThis is great news. Could you let me know which products and roughly how many units you could provide, so we can feature them properly as prizes and plan the on-site presentation and shipping? We'll of course give Chessnut strong visibility across the festival (banners, photo wall, website, mentions during the broadcast and in articles).\n\n2) Boards in the live broadcast\nWe really like the idea of showcasing Chessnut boards live, and since this would be a first, the best starting point is to understand your side. Our games are broadcast live online (https://www.google.com/url?q=http://chess.com&source=gmail&ust=1782396421527000&sa=E / Lichess) alongside the on-site video production. Could you tell us what your boards offer for live tournament broadcasting — how they relay the games and to which platforms (for example Lichess Broadcast / PGN relay)? With that, we can quickly map out how to feature Chessnut on a set of boards and take it from there.\n\nKeeping everything in writing is perfectly fine for me as well.\n\nThank you again, Stella — I'm excited about the possibilities and look forward to your reply.\n\nBest regards,\nMilan Roman\nTournament Director – Chess Slovak Open\nFIDE International Organizer\nPresident of the Slovak Chess Federation\n+421 905 410 990\nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=http://www.chessslovakopen.sk&source=gmail&ust=1782396421528000&sa=E=",
